{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MKRVm2cVVdoyFKwJrphc9H","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Workbook assembly, review, repair, and release: D24-D32 of spec section 6.2.\n2\t\n3\tThis is the one workbook engine (spec section 15's `node_ownership.v1.md`\n4\tresolution): exact manifest coverage (D24), assembly (D25), render/inventory/\n5\tinspection (D26), review-packet freeze (D27), evidence reduction (D28),\n6\tworkbook-only defect classification/planning (D29), admission/retest (D31),\n7\tand final release recomputation (D32) -- plus the two product-terminal call\n8\tsites `D24` (one-mode `UNIT_ACCEPTED`) and `D32` (`COMPLETE`) reach.\n9\t\n10\tLike `repair.py`/`acceptance.py`, none of these functions carries a\n11\t`NODE_CATALOGUE` row: D24-D32 are not narrowed by `nodes.deterministic_node()`\n12\tand are registered into the compiled graph by `register_workbook_path()`\n13\tbelow, called from `graph.py`. A product terminal is never written here --\n14\t`D24`/`D32` only ever produce a `terminal_candidate` and a `pending_guard`\n15\tthat routes to the one real `D98_WRITE_TERMINAL` (owned by\n16\t`nodes/terminal.py`); this module contains no terminal writer and cannot\n17\treach `END` directly.\n18\t\n19\tWorkbook repair is boundary-scoped to the four workbook-owned components\n20\t(`front_matter`, `navigation`, `layout`, `assembly` -- `model_nodes\n21\t.WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS`) and can never stage a writable unit source or\n22\tPDF: `D31` recomputes and compares every accepted unit's frozen PDF hash\n23\tbefore and after a repair candidate is admitted, and any change is a system\n24\tfailure, never a routed finding (spec section 12: \"Workbook repair cannot\n25\tstage writable unit sources or PDFs\").\n26\t\n27\tOnly `D30_CLASSIFY_PREREQUISITE` (owned by N22's `nodes/sources.py`) may ever\n28\tpropose `PAUSED_PREREQUISITE`; nothing in this module does, and `D98`\n29\tindependently re-derives every candidate's precondition regardless of which\n30\tguard proposed it.\n31\t\"\"\"\n32\t\n33\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n34\t\n35\tfrom collections.abc import Mapping, Sequence\n36\tfrom pathlib import Path\n37\tfrom typing import Any\n38\t\n39\tfrom . import repair\n40\tfrom .nodes import (\n41\t    SystemFailure,\n42\t    canonical_digest,\n43\t    candidate_payload,\n44\t    check_record,\n45\t    contract_reference,\n46\t    require,\n47\t    sha256_file,\n48\t    staged_dispatch,\n49\t    stream_id,\n50\t    worker_packet,\n51\t)\n52\t\n53\t__all__ = [\n54\t    \"WORKBOOK_STREAM\",\n55\t    \"WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS\",\n56\t    \"DETERMINISTIC_ONLY_COMPONENTS\",\n57\t    \"MODEL_ONLY_COMPONENTS\",\n58\t    \"WorkbookDenominatorResult\",\n59\t    \"compute_workbook_denominator\",\n60\t    \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\",\n61\t    \"D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\",\n62\t    \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\",\n63\t    \"D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\",\n64\t    \"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\",\n65\t    \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\",\n66\t    \"D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\",\n67\t    \"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\",\n68\t    \"WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES\",\n69\t    \"WORKBOOK_TOPOLOGY_SOURCES\",\n70\t    \"register_workbook_path\",\n71\t]\n72\t\n73\t\n74\t# The one workbook stream: unlike a unit, there is exactly one workbook per\n75\t# episode, so `workbook_head`/`workbook_versions` key on this single name\n76\t# rather than a per-entity stream id the way `nodes.stream_id` mints one.\n77\tWORKBOOK_STREAM = \"workbook\"\n78\t\n79\tWORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS: frozenset[str] = frozenset(\n80\t    {\"front_matter\", \"navigation\", \"layout\", \"assembly\"}\n81\t)\n82\t\n83\t# Spec section 12's workbook row: \"deterministic assembly/template repair\n84\t# first; M08 only for the exact workbook-owned component\". `layout` and\n85\t# `assembly` are the two components a deterministic re-render/re-assemble can\n86\t# regenerate outright (the same renderer D25 already calls); `front_matter`\n87\t# and `navigation` are authored text with no deterministic producer in this\n88\t# generation, so they are M08-eligible. This mirrors unit repair's\n89\t# `DETERMINISTIC_ONLY_OWNERS`/`MODEL_ONLY_OWNERS` split (`repair.py`) rather\n90\t# than inventing a second policy shape.\n91\tDETERMINISTIC_ONLY_COMPONENTS: frozenset[str] = frozenset({\"layout\", \"assembly\"})\n92\tMODEL_ONLY_COMPONENTS: frozenset[str] = frozenset({\"front_matter\", \"navigation\"})\n93\t\n94\tDETERMINISTIC_REPAIR_CANDIDATE_KIND = \"deterministic_workbook_repair_candidate\"\n95\t\n96\t# The one body section each workbook-owned component's repair is scoped to.\n97\t# `layout` and `assembly` share `/assembly` deliberately (spec section 12:\n98\t# both are re-rendered together); `/coverage` -- the accepted-unit hash\n99\t# ledger -- is named by no component, which is exactly the unit-byte\n100\t# immutability guarantee D31 also re-derives independently.\n101\t_COMPONENT_BODY_POINTER: dict[str, str] = {\n102\t    \"front_matter\": \"/front_matter\",\n103\t    \"navigation\": \"/navigation\",\n104\t    \"layout\": \"/assembly\",\n105\t    \"assembly\": \"/assembly\",\n106\t}\n107\t\n108\t# Frozen limits reused from the one repair engine (spec section 12: \"shared\n109\t# boundary/diff/invalidation-DAG machinery reused by workbook repair\") --\n110\t# never redeclared with a different value here.\n111\tMAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = repair.MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN\n112\tMAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS = repair.MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS\n113\t\n114\t\n115\tdef _guard(node_id: str, value: str, **detail: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n116\t    return {\"node\": node_id, \"value\": value, \"detail\": detail}\n117\t\n118\t\n119\tdef _record(value: Any, label: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n120\t    require(isinstance(value, Mapping), \"schema_contract\", f\"{label} must be a JSON object\")\n121\t    return dict(value)\n122\t\n123\t\n124\tdef _accepted_pdf_hash(receipt: Any, unit_id: str) -> str:\n125\t    require(isinstance(receipt, Mapping), \"integrity\", f\"unit {unit_id!r} has no accepted receipt\")\n126\t    pages = ((receipt.get(\"denominator\") or {}).get(\"pages\")) or {}\n127\t    pdf_sha256 = pages.get(\"pdf_sha256\")\n128\t    require(\n129\t        isinstance(pdf_sha256, str) and bool(pdf_sha256),\n130\t        \"integrity\",\n131\t        f\"the accepted receipt for {unit_id!r} carries no frozen unit pdf hash\",\n132\t    )\n133\t    return pdf_sha256\n134\t\n135\t\n136\tdef _latest_workbook_version(workbook_versions: Any, workbook_hash: str) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n137\t    matches = [\n138\t        dict(record)\n139\t        for record in workbook_versions or []\n140\t        if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n141\t        and record.get(\"hash\") == workbook_hash\n142\t        and record.get(\"record_kind\") is None\n143\t    ]\n144\t    return matches[-1] if matches else None\n145\t\n146\t\n147\tdef _latest_model_repair_candidate(workbook_versions: Any) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n148\t    matches = [\n149\t        dict(record)\n150\t        for record in workbook_versions or []\n151\t        if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n152\t        and record.get(\"record_kind\") == \"model_candidate\"\n153\t        and record.get(\"job_id\") == \"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\"\n154\t    ]\n155\t    return matches[-1] if matches else None\n156\t\n157\t\n158\tdef _latest_deterministic_repair_candidate(\n159\t    workbook_versions: Any, *, request_key: str\n160\t) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n161\t    matches = [\n162\t        dict(record)\n163\t        for record in workbook_versions or []\n164\t        if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n165\t        and record.get(\"record_kind\") == DETERMINISTIC_REPAIR_CANDIDATE_KIND\n166\t        and record.get(\"request_key\") == request_key\n167\t    ]\n168\t    return matches[-1] if matches else None\n169\t\n170\t\n171\tdef _latest_workbook_review(workbook_reviews: Any, workbook_pdf_sha256: str | None) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n172\t    if not workbook_pdf_sha256:\n173\t        return None\n174\t    matches = [\n175\t        dict(record)\n176\t        for record in workbook_reviews or []\n177\t        if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n178\t        and record.get(\"record_kind\") == \"model_candidate\"\n179\t        and record.get(\"job_id\") == \"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\"\n180\t        and record.get(\"workbook_pdf_sha256\") == workbook_pdf_sha256\n181\t    ]\n182\t    return matches[-1] if matches else None\n183\t\n184\t\n185\tdef _attempt_key(fingerprint: str) -> str:\n186\t    return f\"workbook_repair|{fingerprint}\"\n187\t\n188\t\n189\tdef _repeat_key(fingerprint: str) -> str:\n190\t    return f\"workbook_repeat|{fingerprint}\"\n191\t\n192\t\n193\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n194\t# D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\n195\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n196\t\n197\t\n198\tdef D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n199\t    \"\"\"One-mode unit terminal, or all-mode exact ordered coverage proof.\"\"\"\n200\t\n201\t    mode = state.get(\"mode\")\n202\t    require(mode in (\"one\", \"all\"), \"invalid_input\", \"D24 requires a decided run mode\")\n203\t\n204\t    effective_run = state.get(\"effective_run\") or {}\n205\t    closure = list(effective_run.get(\"target_closure\") or [])\n206\t    require(bool(closure), \"invalid_input\", \"D24 requires a non-empty frozen target closure\")\n207\t    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n208\t\n209\t    missing = [unit_id for unit_id in closure if unit_id not in accepted]\n210\t    require(\n211\t        not missing,\n212\t        \"integrity\",\n213\t        \"D24 requires an accepted receipt for every unit in the frozen closure\",\n214\t        missing=missing,\n215\t    )\n216\t\n217\t    if mode == \"one\":\n218\t        requested = state.get(\"requested_unit_id\")\n219\t        require(\n220\t            isinstance(requested, str) and requested in accepted,\n221\t            \"integrity\",\n222\t            \"the requested unit has no accepted receipt\",\n223\t            requested_unit_id=requested,\n224\t        )\n225\t        require(requested in closure, \"integrity\", \"the requested unit is outside the frozen closure\")\n226\t        receipt = accepted[requested]\n227\t        checkpoints = state.get(\"checkpoint_metadata\") or []\n228\t        require(bool(checkpoints), \"integrity\", \"D24 requires a current checkpoint correlation\")\n229\t        checkpoint_id = checkpoints[-1].get(\"checkpoint_id\")\n230\t\n231\t        candidate = {\n232\t            \"kind\": \"UNIT_ACCEPTED\",\n233\t            \"unit_id\": requested,\n234\t            \"receipt_hash\": receipt[\"receipt_hash\"],\n235\t            \"closure_receipt_hashes\": {unit_id: accepted[unit_id][\"receipt_hash\"] for unit_id in closure},\n236\t            \"denominator\": receipt[\"denominator\"],\n237\t            \"log_high_water_mark\": len(state.get(\"evidence_index_entries\") or []),\n238\t            \"checkpoint_id\": checkpoint_id,\n239\t        }\n240\t        return {\n241\t            \"terminal_candidate\": candidate,\n242\t            \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n243\t                \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\", \"unit_target_accepted\", unit_id=requested\n244\t            ),\n245\t        }\n246\t\n247\t    ordered = list(effective_run.get(\"ordered_unit_ids\") or [])\n248\t    require(bool(ordered), \"invalid_input\", \"D24 requires a non-empty frozen manifest order\")\n249\t    require(\n250\t        sorted(ordered) == sorted(closure) and len(ordered) == len(closure),\n251\t        \"integrity\",\n252\t        \"full-mode manifest order and target closure disagree\",\n253\t        ordered=ordered,\n254\t        closure=closure,\n255\t    )\n256\t\n257\t    declared_coverage = [{\"unit_id\": unit_id, \"receipt_hash\": accepted[unit_id][\"receipt_hash\"]} for unit_id in ordered]\n258\t    ok, rejections = repair_acceptance_coverage_proof(ordered, accepted, declared_coverage)\n259\t    require(ok, \"integrity\", \"exact manifest coverage failed\", rejections=rejections)\n260\t\n261\t    coverage_record = {\n262\t        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"kind\": \"workbook_coverage\", \"ordered_unit_ids\": ordered, \"declared_coverage\": declared_coverage}),\n263\t        \"ordered_unit_ids\": ordered,\n264\t        \"receipt_hashes\": {unit_id: accepted[unit_id][\"receipt_hash\"] for unit_id in ordered},\n265\t    }\n266\t    return {\n267\t        \"workbook_coverage\": [coverage_record],\n268\t        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n269\t            \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\", \"manifest_coverage_proven\", ordered_unit_ids=ordered\n270\t        ),\n271\t    }\n272\t\n273\t\n274\tdef repair_acceptance_coverage_proof(\n275\t    ordered_unit_ids: Sequence[str],\n276\t    accepted_unit_receipts: Mapping[str, Any],\n277\t    declared_coverage: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]],\n278\t) -> tuple[bool, list[str]]:\n279\t    \"\"\"The exact coverage predicate (spec section 13.2 item 1), applied at D24.\n280\t\n281\t    Delegates to N31's `acceptance.prove_exact_manifest_coverage` -- one\n282\t    coverage rule, not a second copy of it -- imported lazily to avoid a\n283\t    module cycle (`acceptance.py` itself imports `repair`, and this module\n284\t    imports `repair` at top level).\n285\t    \"\"\"\n286\t\n287\t    from . import acceptance\n288\t\n289\t    return acceptance.prove_exact_manifest_coverage(\n290\t        list(ordered_unit_ids), accepted_unit_receipts, list(declared_coverage)\n291\t    )\n292\t\n293\t\n294\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n295\t# D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\n296\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n297\t\n298\t\n299\tdef D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n300\t    \"\"\"Assemble the workbook over exact accepted receipts and immutable unit PDFs.\n301\t\n302\t    Never mutates a unit: every unit PDF byte this reads is re-verified against\n303\t    the hash the unit's own accepted receipt froze, both the version D25 sees\n304\t    in state and the actual bytes on disk, before assembly proceeds.\n305\t    \"\"\"\n306\t\n307\t    coverage_entries = [\n308\t        record for record in state.get(\"workbook_coverage\") or [] if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n309\t    ]\n310\t    require(bool(coverage_entries), \"invalid_input\", \"D25 requires a proven coverage record\")\n311\t    coverage = coverage_entries[-1]\n312\t    ordered = list(coverage[\"ordered_unit_ids\"])\n313\t    receipt_hashes = dict(coverage[\"receipt_hashes\"])\n314\t    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n315\t    artifact_versions = state.get(\"artifact_versions\") or []\n316\t\n317\t    unit_pdf_hashes: dict[str, str] = {}\n318\t    for unit_id in ordered:\n319\t        receipt = accepted.get(unit_id)\n320\t        require(\n321\t            isinstance(receipt, Mapping) and receipt.get(\"receipt_hash\") == receipt_hashes.get(unit_id),\n322\t            \"integrity\",\n323\t            \"the proven coverage receipt hash is not the current accepted receipt\",\n324\t            unit_id=unit_id,\n325\t        )\n326\t        accepted_pdf_sha256 = _accepted_pdf_hash(receipt, unit_id)\n327\t\n328\t        layout_stream = stream_id(unit_id, \"layout\")\n329\t        layout_candidates = [\n330\t            dict(record)\n331\t            for record in artifact_versions\n332\t            if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"stream\") == layout_stream\n333\t        ]\n334\t        require(bool(layout_candidates), \"integrity\", f\"no rendered layout exists for accepted unit {unit_id!r}\")\n335\t        layout_version = max(layout_candidates, key=lambda record: record.get(\"version\", 0))\n336\t        require(\n337\t            layout_version.get(\"pdf_sha256\") == accepted_pdf_sha256,\n338\t            \"integrity\",\n339\t            \"unit PDF bytes changed after acceptance\",\n340\t            unit_id=unit_id,\n341\t            accepted=accepted_pdf_sha256,\n342\t            current=layout_version.get(\"pdf_sha256\"),\n343\t        )\n344\t        pdf_path = Path(str(layout_version.get(\"pdf_path\")))\n345\t        require(pdf_path.is_file(), \"integrity\", \"the accepted unit PDF is missing\", unit_id=unit_id)\n346\t        actual = sha256_file(pdf_path)\n347\t        require(\n348\t            actual == accepted_pdf_sha256,\n349\t            \"integrity\",\n350\t            \"the unit PDF bytes on disk no longer match the accepted hash\",\n351\t            unit_id=unit_id,\n352\t        )\n353\t        unit_pdf_hashes[unit_id] = accepted_pdf_sha256\n354\t\n355\t    engine_root = state.get(\"engine_root\")\n356\t    front_matter = contract_reference(engine_root, \"meta_prompt/assets/pedagogy.v1.md\")\n357\t\n358\t    registry = getattr(runtime_context, \"transport_registry\", None)\n359\t    assembler = getattr(registry, \"assemble_workbook\", None) if registry else None\n360\t    require(callable(assembler), \"capability\", \"runtime context exposes no workbook assembler\")\n361\t    try:\n362\t        assembled = assembler(ordered, unit_pdf_hashes, front_matter)\n363\t    except Exception as error:  # noqa: BLE001 - a tool fault is always a system failure\n364\t        raise SystemFailure(\n365\t            \"tool\", f\"workbook assembly failed: {error}\", {\"ordered_unit_ids\": ordered}\n366\t        ) from error\n367\t\n368\t    result = _record(assembled, \"workbook assembly result\")\n369\t    for field in (\"workbook_pdf_path\", \"workbook_pdf_sha256\", \"assembly_map\", \"navigation\"):\n370\t        require(field in result, \"integrity\", f\"workbook assembly result has no {field!r}\")\n371\t    assembly_map = result[\"assembly_map\"]\n372\t    require(\n373\t        isinstance(assembly_map, list) and [entry.get(\"unit_id\") for entry in assembly_map] == ordered,\n374\t        \"integrity\",\n375\t        \"the assembly map is not exactly the proven coverage order\",\n376\t        expected=ordered,\n377\t    )\n378\t    for entry in assembly_map:\n379\t        entry_record = _record(entry, \"assembly map entry\")\n380\t        require(\n381\t            entry_record.get(\"unit_pdf_sha256\") == unit_pdf_hashes.get(entry_record.get(\"unit_id\")),\n382\t            \"integrity\",\n383\t            \"the assembly map cites a unit pdf hash the coverage did not prove\",\n384\t            unit_id=entry_record.get(\"unit_id\"),\n385\t        )\n386\t\n387\t    body = {\n388\t        \"front_matter\": front_matter,\n389\t        \"navigation\": result[\"navigation\"],\n390\t        \"coverage\": {\"ordered_unit_ids\": ordered, \"unit_pdf_hashes\": unit_pdf_hashes},\n391\t        \"assembly\": {\n392\t            \"assembly_map\": assembly_map,\n393\t            \"workbook_pdf_path\": result[\"workbook_pdf_path\"],\n394\t            \"workbook_pdf_sha256\": result[\"workbook_pdf_sha256\"],\n395\t        },\n396\t    }\n397\t\n398\t    current_head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM) or {}\n399\t    version_record = {\n400\t        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"kind\": \"workbook_version\", \"body\": body, \"parent\": current_head.get(\"hash\")}),\n401\t        \"record_kind\": None,\n402\t        \"version\": int(current_head.get(\"version\", 0)) + 1,\n403\t        \"parent_hash\": current_head.get(\"hash\"),\n404\t        \"hash\": canonical_digest(body),\n405\t        \"body\": body,\n406\t    }\n407\t\n408\t    return {\n409\t        \"workbook_versions\": [version_record],\n410\t        \"workbook_head\": {\n411\t            WORKBOOK_STREAM: {\n412\t                \"version\": version_record[\"version\"],\n413\t                \"parent_hash\": version_record[\"parent_hash\"],\n414\t                \"hash\": version_record[\"hash\"],\n415\t            }\n416\t        },\n417\t        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\", \"workbook_assembled\"),\n418\t    }\n419\t\n420\t\n421\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n422\t# D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\n423\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n424\t\n425\t\n426\tdef D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n427\t    \"\"\"Prove a positive contiguous workbook page inventory and inspect every page.\"\"\"\n428\t\n429\t    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n430\t    require(isinstance(head, Mapping), \"invalid_input\", \"D26 requires an assembled workbook head\")\n431\t    version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"])\n432\t    require(isinstance(version, Mapping), \"integrity\", \"no admitted workbook version matches the current head\")\n433\t\n434\t    assembly = version[\"body\"][\"assembly\"]\n435\t    pdf_sha256 = assembly[\"workbook_pdf_sha256\"]\n436\t    pdf_path = Path(str(assembly[\"workbook_pdf_path\"]))\n437\t    require(pdf_path.is_file(), \"integrity\", \"the assembled workbook PDF is missing\")\n438\t    actual = sha256_file(pdf_path)\n439\t    require(\n440\t        actual == pdf_sha256,\n441\t        \"integrity\",\n442\t        \"the workbook PDF bytes changed after assembly\",\n443\t        declared=pdf_sha256,\n444\t        actual=actual,\n445\t    )\n446\t\n447\t    registry = getattr(runtime_context, \"transport_registry\", None)\n448\t    inspector = getattr(registry, \"inspect_workbook_pages\", None) if registry else None\n449\t    require(callable(inspector), \"capability\", \"runtime context exposes no workbook page inspector\")\n450\t    try:\n451\t        inspected = inspector(str(pdf_path), pdf_sha256)\n452\t    except Exception as error:  # noqa: BLE001 - a rasterizer/tool fault is always a system failure\n453\t        raise SystemFailure(\n454\t            \"tool\", f\"workbook page inspection failed: {error}\", {\"pdf_sha256\": pdf_sha256}\n455\t        ) from error\n456\t\n457\t    report = _record(inspected, \"workbook page inspection\")\n458\t    pages = report.get(\"pages\")\n459\t    require(isinstance(pages, list), \"schema_contract\", \"workbook page inspection returned a non-list page set\")\n460\t\n461\t    numbers = [page.get(\"number\") for page in pages if isinstance(page, Mapping)]\n462\t    contiguous = numbers == list(range(1, len(pages) + 1))\n463\t    positive = len(pages) > 0\n464\t\n465\t    inventory = {\n466\t        \"key\": f\"workbook/{pdf_sha256}\",\n467\t        \"pdf_sha256\": pdf_sha256,\n468\t        \"page_count\": len(pages),\n469\t        \"contiguous\": contiguous,\n470\t        \"result\": \"PASS\" if positive and contiguous else \"FAIL\",\n471\t    }\n472\t\n473\t    inspections: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n474\t    findings: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n475\t    if not (positive and contiguous):\n476\t        findings.append(\n477\t            {\n478\t                \"component\": \"layout\",\n479\t                \"check_id\": \"workbook_page_inventory\",\n480\t                \"pointer\": \"/assembly/pages\",\n481\t                \"message\": \"page inventory is empty\" if not positive else f\"page numbering is not 1..N: {numbers}\",\n482\t            }\n483\t        )\n484\t\n485\t    for page in pages:\n486\t        page_record = _record(page, \"workbook page inspection entry\")\n487\t        number = page_record.get(\"number\")\n488\t        problems = sorted(str(item) for item in page_record.get(\"problems\", []) or [])\n489\t        if bool(page_record.get(\"unreadable\")):\n490\t            problems = sorted({*problems, \"unreadable\"})\n491\t        page_sha256 = page_record.get(\"page_sha256\")\n492\t        require(\n493\t            isinstance(page_sha256, str) and len(page_sha256) == 64,\n494\t            \"integrity\",\n495\t            f\"workbook page {number} was inspected without a page hash\",\n496\t        )\n497\t        image_path = page_record.get(\"image_path\")\n498\t        require(\n499\t            isinstance(image_path, str) and bool(image_path),\n500\t            \"integrity\",\n501\t            f\"workbook page {number} was inspected without a rendered page image\",\n502\t        )\n503\t        inspections.append(\n504\t            {\n505\t                \"key\": f\"workbook/{pdf_sha256}/{number}\",\n506\t                \"pdf_sha256\": pdf_sha256,\n507\t                \"page\": number,\n508\t                \"page_sha256\": page_sha256,\n509\t                \"image_path\": image_path,\n510\t                \"problems\": problems,\n511\t                \"result\": \"PASS\" if not problems else \"FAIL\",\n512\t            }\n513\t        )\n514\t        if problems:\n515\t            findings.append(\n516\t                {\n517\t                    \"component\": \"layout\",\n518\t                    \"check_id\": \"workbook_page_inspection\",\n519\t                    \"pointer\": f\"/assembly/pages/{number}\",\n520\t                    \"message\": f\"workbook page {number} failed inspection: {problems}\",\n521\t                }\n522\t            )\n523\t\n524\t    check = check_record(\n525\t        scope=\"workbook\",\n526\t        owner=WORKBOOK_STREAM,\n527\t        head_hash=pdf_sha256,\n528\t        check_id=\"workbook_pages_inspected\",\n529\t        attempt=version.get(\"version\", 1),\n530\t        result=\"PASS\" if not findings else \"FAIL\",\n531\t        detail={\"page_count\": len(pages), \"finding_count\": len(findings)},\n532\t    )\n533\t\n534\t    value = \"workbook_pages_inspected\" if not findings else \"workbook_layout_repairable\"\n535\t    return {\n536\t        \"workbook_page_inventories\": [inventory],\n537\t        \"workbook_page_inspections\": inspections,\n538\t        \"deterministic_checks\": [check],\n539\t        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n540\t            \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\", value, findings=findings\n541\t        ),\n542\t    }\n543\t\n544\t\n545\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n546\t# D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\n547\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n548\t\n549\t\n550\tdef D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n551\t    \"\"\"Freeze the immutable workbook review packet, exactly every page included.\"\"\"\n552\t\n553\t    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n554\t    require(isinstance(head, Mapping), \"invalid_input\", \"D27 requires an assembled workbook head\")\n555\t    version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"])\n556\t    require(isinstance(version, Mapping), \"integrity\", \"no admitted workbook version matches the current head\")\n557\t    body = version[\"body\"]\n558\t\n559\t    inventories = [\n560\t        record\n561\t        for record in state.get(\"workbook_page_inventories\") or []\n562\t        if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"pdf_sha256\") == body[\"assembly\"][\"workbook_pdf_sha256\"]\n563\t    ]\n564\t    require(bool(inventories), \"invalid_input\", \"D27 requires a current workbook page inventory\")\n565\t    inventory = max(inventories, key=lambda record: record.get(\"page_count\", 0))\n566\t    pdf_sha256 = inventory[\"pdf_sha256\"]\n567\t\n568\t    inspections = sorted(\n569\t        (\n570\t            record\n571\t            for record in state.get(\"workbook_page_inspections\") or []\n572\t            if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"pdf_sha256\") == pdf_sha256\n573\t        ),\n574\t        key=lambda record: record.get(\"page\", 0),\n575\t    )\n576\t    page_numbers = [record.get(\"page\") for record in inspections]\n577\t    require(\n578\t        page_numbers == list(range(1, inventory[\"page_count\"] + 1)),\n579\t        \"join\",\n580\t        \"the frozen packet's page set is not exactly the inventory's pages\",\n581\t        expected=inventory[\"page_count\"],\n582\t        actual=page_numbers,\n583\t    )\n584\t\n585\t    pdf_path = Path(str(body[\"assembly\"][\"workbook_pdf_path\"]))\n586\t    require(pdf_path.is_file(), \"integrity\", \"the shipped workbook PDF is missing\")\n587\t    actual = sha256_file(pdf_path)\n588\t    require(\n589\t        actual == pdf_sha256,\n590\t        \"integrity\",\n591\t        \"the shipped workbook PDF bytes do not match the inventoried hash\",\n592\t    )\n593\t\n594\t    checks = [\n595\t        record\n596\t        for record in state.get(\"deterministic_checks\") or []\n597\t        if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"scope\") == \"workbook\"\n598\t    ]\n599\t\n600\t    rubric_path = Path(str(state.get(\"engine_root\"))) / \"meta_prompt\" / \"assets\" / \"pedagogy.v1.md\"\n601\t    rubric = {\"path\": str(rubric_path), \"sha256\": sha256_file(rubric_path) if rubric_path.is_file() else None}\n602\t    require(rubric[\"sha256\"] is not None, \"schema_contract\", \"the workbook review rubric is missing\")\n603\t\n604\t    coverage_entries = [\n605\t        record for record in state.get(\"workbook_coverage\") or [] if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n606\t    ]\n607\t    require(bool(coverage_entries), \"invalid_input\", \"D27 requires a proven coverage record\")\n608\t    coverage = coverage_entries[-1]\n609\t\n610\t    packet = {\n611\t        \"coverage_map\": {\n612\t            \"ordered_unit_ids\": list(coverage[\"ordered_unit_ids\"]),\n613\t            \"receipt_hashes\": dict(coverage[\"receipt_hashes\"]),\n614\t        },\n615\t        \"accepted_unit_hashes\": dict(body[\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"]),\n616\t        \"workbook_pdf_sha256\": pdf_sha256,\n617\t        \"page_count\": inventory[\"page_count\"],\n618\t        \"page_keys\": [record[\"key\"] for record in inspections],\n619\t        \"deterministic_check_keys\": sorted(\n620\t            f\"{record['scope']}/{record['owner']}/{record['head_hash']}/{record['check_id']}/{record['attempt']}\"\n621\t            for record in checks\n622\t        ),\n623\t        \"rubric\": rubric,\n624\t    }\n625\t    packet[\"denominator\"] = {\"pages\": inventory[\"page_count\"], \"checks\": len(packet[\"deterministic_check_keys\"])}\n626\t    packet[\"key\"] = canonical_digest(packet)\n627\t    packet[\"packet_hash\"] = packet[\"key\"]\n628\t\n629\t    page_records = []\n630\t    for record in inspections:\n631\t        page_records.append(\n632\t            {\n633\t                \"page_number\": record[\"page\"],\n634\t                \"page_sha256\": record[\"page_sha256\"],\n635\t                \"image_path\": record[\"image_path\"],\n636\t            }\n637\t        )\n638\t\n639\t    review_worker_packet = worker_packet(\n640\t        run_id=state.get(\"run_id\"),\n641\t        episode_id=state.get(\"episode_id\"),\n642\t        correlation_key=f\"workbook/{pdf_sha256}/review\",\n643\t        projection={\n644\t            \"coverage_map\": dict(packet[\"coverage_map\"]),\n645\t            \"accepted_unit_hashes\": dict(packet[\"accepted_unit_hashes\"]),\n646\t            \"workbook_pdf\": {\"sha256\": pdf_sha256, \"path\": str(pdf_path)},\n647\t            \"page_inventory\": {\n648\t                \"page_count\": inventory[\"page_count\"],\n649\t                \"pages\": [\n650\t                    {\"page_number\": entry[\"page_number\"], \"page_sha256\": entry[\"page_sha256\"]}\n651\t                    for entry in page_records\n652\t                ],\n653\t            },\n654\t            \"pages\": page_records,\n655\t            \"deterministic_evidence\": [\n656\t                {\n657\t                    \"check_id\": record[\"check_id\"],\n658\t                    \"scope\": record[\"scope\"],\n659\t                    \"head_hash\": record[\"head_hash\"],\n660\t                    \"result\": record[\"result\"],\n661\t                }\n662\t                for record in checks\n663\t            ],\n664\t            \"rubric\": dict(rubric),\n665\t        },\n666\t    )\n667\t\n668\t    return {\n669\t        \"workbook_review_packets\": [packet],\n670\t        \"pending_packet\": staged_dispatch(\"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\", [review_worker_packet]),\n671\t        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\", \"workbook_packet_frozen\"),\n672\t    }\n673\t\n674\t\n675\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n676\t# Denominator (shared shape by D28 and D32 -- spec section 13.2)\n677\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n678\t\n679\t\n680\tclass WorkbookDenominatorResult:\n681\t    __slots__ = (\"passed\", \"check\", \"findings\", \"denominator\")\n682\t\n683\t    def __init__(\n684\t        self,\n685\t        passed: bool,\n686\t        check: dict[str, Any],\n687\t        findings: list[dict[str, Any]],\n688\t        denominator: dict[str, Any],\n689\t    ) -> None:\n690\t        self.passed = passed\n691\t        self.check = check\n692\t        self.findings = findings\n693\t        self.denominator = denominator\n694\t\n695\t\n696\tdef compute_workbook_denominator(state: Mapping[str, Any]) -> WorkbookDenominatorResult:\n697\t    \"\"\"Recompute the complete current workbook denominator (spec section 13.2).\n698\t\n699\t    Never trusts a cached pass label: every category below is re-derived from\n700\t    the *current* state on every call, exactly as `acceptance\n701\t    .compute_unit_denominator` does for a unit -- a stale head, a superseded\n702\t    review, or an unresolved workbook repair request all fail this function\n703\t    freshly regardless of what an earlier call over older state returned.\n704\t    \"\"\"\n705\t\n706\t    findings: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n707\t    categories: dict[str, Any] = {}\n708\t\n709\t    def _fail(component: str, check_id: str, pointer: str, message: str) -> None:\n710\t        findings.append({\"check_id\": check_id, \"component\": component, \"pointer\": pointer, \"message\": message})\n711\t\n712\t    effective_run = state.get(\"effective_run\") or {}\n713\t    ordered = list(effective_run.get(\"ordered_unit_ids\") or [])\n714\t    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n715\t    coverage_entries = [record for record in state.get(\"workbook_coverage\") or [] if isinstance(record, Mapping)]\n716\t    coverage = coverage_entries[-1] if coverage_entries else None\n717\t\n718\t    coverage_ok = (\n719\t        coverage is not None\n720\t        and list(coverage.get(\"ordered_unit_ids\") or []) == ordered\n721\t        and bool(ordered)\n722\t        and all(\n723\t            isinstance(accepted.get(unit_id), Mapping)\n724\t            and accepted[unit_id].get(\"receipt_hash\") == coverage.get(\"receipt_hashes\", {}).get(unit_id)\n725\t            for unit_id in ordered\n726\t        )\n727\t    )\n728\t    categories[\"coverage\"] = {\"result\": \"PASS\" if coverage_ok else \"FAIL\"}\n729\t    if not coverage_ok:\n730\t        _fail(\"assembly\", \"workbook_coverage\", \"/coverage\", \"current coverage is not exact ordered full-manifest membership\")\n731\t\n732\t    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n733\t    version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"]) if isinstance(head, Mapping) else None\n734\t    unit_bytes_ok = coverage_ok and version is not None\n735\t    if unit_bytes_ok:\n736\t        for unit_id, pdf_sha256 in version[\"body\"][\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"].items():\n737\t            receipt = accepted.get(unit_id)\n738\t            if not isinstance(receipt, Mapping) or ((receipt.get(\"denominator\") or {}).get(\"pages\") or {}).get(\"pdf_sha256\") != pdf_sha256:\n739\t                unit_bytes_ok = False\n740\t                break\n741\t    categories[\"unit_bytes\"] = {\"result\": \"PASS\" if unit_bytes_ok else \"FAIL\"}\n742\t    if not unit_bytes_ok:\n743\t        _fail(\"assembly\", \"workbook_unit_bytes\", \"/assembly\", \"an accepted unit's PDF bytes are not the assembled workbook's frozen bytes\")\n744\t\n745\t    pdf_sha256 = version[\"body\"][\"assembly\"][\"workbook_pdf_sha256\"] if version is not None else None\n746\t    inventories = [\n747\t        record\n748\t        for record in state.get(\"workbook_page_inventories\") or []\n749\t        if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"pdf_sha256\") == pdf_sha256\n750\t    ]\n751\t    inventory = max(inventories, key=lambda record: record.get(\"page_count\", 0)) if inventories else None\n752\t    inventory_ok = isinstance(inventory, Mapping) and inventory.get(\"result\") == \"PASS\"\n753\t    inspections = [\n754\t        record\n755\t        for record in state.get(\"workbook_page_inspections\") or []\n756\t        if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"pdf_sha256\") == pdf_sha256\n757\t    ]\n758\t    expected_pages = inventory.get(\"page_count\") if isinstance(inventory, Mapping) else -1\n759\t    pages_ok = inventory_ok and len(inspections) == expected_pages and all(record.get(\"result\") == \"PASS\" for record in inspections)\n760\t    categories[\"pages\"] = {\"result\": \"PASS\" if pages_ok else \"FAIL\", \"pdf_sha256\": pdf_sha256, \"page_count\": expected_pages}\n761\t    if not pages_ok:\n762\t        _fail(\"layout\", \"workbook_pages\", \"/assembly/pages\", \"the workbook page inventory/inspection set is not current and fully passing\")\n763\t\n764\t    review = _latest_workbook_review(state.get(\"workbook_reviews\"), pdf_sha256)\n765\t    review_ok = review is not None\n766\t    if review is not None:\n767\t        payload = candidate_payload(review, \"workbook review\")\n768\t        blocking = [\n769\t            entry for entry in payload.get(\"overall_findings\", [])\n770\t            if isinstance(entry, Mapping) and entry.get(\"severity\") == \"blocking\"\n771\t        ]\n772\t        for page_entry in payload.get(\"page_findings\", []):\n773\t            if isinstance(page_entry, Mapping):\n774\t                blocking.extend(\n775\t                    entry for entry in page_entry.get(\"findings\", [])\n776\t                    if isinstance(entry, Mapping) and entry.get(\"severity\") == \"blocking\"\n777\t                )\n778\t        for entry in blocking:\n779\t            component = str(entry.get(\"category\") or \"layout\")\n780\t            component = component if component in WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS else \"layout\"\n781\t            findings.append(\n782\t                {\n783\t                    \"check_id\": \"workbook_review_finding\",\n784\t                    \"component\": component,\n785\t                    \"pointer\": entry.get(\"evidence_reference\") or \"/review\",\n786\t                    \"message\": entry.get(\"description\", \"\"),\n787\t                }\n788\t            )\n789\t        review_ok = not blocking\n790\t    categories[\"review\"] = {\"result\": \"PASS\" if review_ok else \"FAIL\", \"present\": review is not None}\n791\t    if review is None:\n792\t        _fail(\"navigation\", \"workbook_review_missing\", \"/review\", \"no independent workbook review candidate is present for the current pdf\")\n793\t\n794\t    open_requests = [\n795\t        record\n796\t        for record in state.get(\"workbook_repair_requests\") or []\n797\t        if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n798\t        and record.get(\"key\")\n799\t        not in {\n800\t            entry.get(\"request_key\")\n801\t            for entry in state.get(\"workbook_retests\") or []\n802\t            if isinstance(entry, Mapping) and entry.get(\"resolved\")\n803\t        }\n804\t    ]\n805\t    repair_ok = not open_requests\n806\t    categories[\"repair\"] = {\"result\": \"PASS\" if repair_ok else \"FAIL\", \"open_requests\": len(open_requests)}\n807\t    if not repair_ok:\n808\t        _fail(open_requests[0][\"component\"], \"workbook_repair_unresolved\", \"/repair\", \"a workbook repair request remains open (not yet retested)\")\n809\t\n810\t    passed = all(entry.get(\"result\") == \"PASS\" for entry in categories.values())\n811\t    summary_hash = canonical_digest({\"kind\": \"workbook_denominator\", \"categories\": categories})\n812\t    check = check_record(\n813\t        scope=\"workbook\",\n814\t        owner=WORKBOOK_STREAM,\n815\t        head_hash=summary_hash,\n816\t        check_id=\"workbook_denominator\",\n817\t        attempt=1,\n818\t        result=\"PASS\" if passed else \"FAIL\",\n819\t        detail={\"categories\": categories},\n820\t    )\n821\t    return WorkbookDenominatorResult(passed, check, findings, categories)\n822\t\n823\t\n824\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n825\t# D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\n826\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n827\t\n828\t\n829\tdef D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n830\t    \"\"\"Build the complete current workbook denominator; release, or open repair.\"\"\"\n831\t\n832\t    result = compute_workbook_denominator(state)\n833\t    if result.passed:\n834\t        return {\n835\t            \"deterministic_checks\": [result.check],\n836\t            \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\", \"workbook_denominator_passed\"),\n837\t        }\n838\t    return {\n839\t        \"deterministic_checks\": [result.check],\n840\t        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n841\t            \"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\", \"workbook_findings_repairable\", findings=result.findings\n842\t        ),\n843\t    }\n844\t\n845\t\n846\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n847\t# D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\n848\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n849\t\n850\t\n851\tdef D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n852\t    \"\"\"Classify the current workbook-only findings and plan exactly one repair.\n853\t\n854\t    Merges spec 6.2's D17/D18/D19 roles into the one row the workbook branch\n855\t    declares: total classification, one planned request, and deterministic-vs-\n856\t    model routing, all against the single `WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS`\n857\t    vocabulary rather than the five-owner unit table.\n858\t    \"\"\"\n859\t\n860\t    guard_record = state.get(\"pending_guard\")\n861\t    pending_failure = state.get(\"pending_failure\")\n862\t\n863\t    if isinstance(pending_failure, Mapping) and pending_failure.get(\"classification\") == \"repair\":\n864\t        detail = pending_failure.get(\"evidence\") if isinstance(pending_failure.get(\"evidence\"), Mapping) else {}\n865\t        raw_findings = [\n866\t            {\n867\t                \"component\": \"front_matter\",\n868\t                \"check_id\": pending_failure.get(\"failure_class\"),\n869\t                \"pointer\": \"/front_matter\",\n870\t                \"message\": pending_failure.get(\"detail\") or pending_failure.get(\"message\") or \"\",\n871\t            }\n872\t        ]\n873\t        source_node = \"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"\n874\t    else:\n875\t        require(isinstance(guard_record, Mapping), \"invalid_input\", \"D29 has no findings to classify\")\n876\t        detail = guard_record.get(\"detail\") if isinstance(guard_record.get(\"detail\"), Mapping) else {}\n877\t        raw_findings = detail.get(\"findings\")\n878\t        require(\n879\t            isinstance(raw_findings, list) and bool(raw_findings),\n880\t            \"invalid_input\",\n881\t            \"D29 was routed with an empty or missing findings list\",\n882\t        )\n883\t        source_node = str(guard_record.get(\"node\") or \"\")\n884\t\n885\t    normalized: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n886\t    for raw in raw_findings:\n887\t        raw_record = _record(raw, \"workbook finding\")\n888\t        component = raw_record.get(\"component\")\n889\t        require(\n890\t            component in WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS,\n891\t            \"invalid_input\",\n892\t            f\"workbook finding declares component {component!r}, which is not one of the four workbook-owned components\",\n893\t        )\n894\t        pointer = raw_record.get(\"pointer\")\n895\t        require(isinstance(pointer, str) and bool(pointer), \"invalid_input\", \"workbook finding declares no boundary pointer\")\n896\t        message = raw_record.get(\"message\", \"\")\n897\t        normalized.append(\n898\t            {\n899\t                \"finding_id\": canonical_digest({\"component\": component, \"pointer\": pointer, \"message\": str(message)}),\n900\t                \"component\": component,\n901\t                \"boundary\": pointer,\n902\t                \"message\": str(message),\n903\t                \"source_node\": source_node,\n904\t            }\n905\t        )\n906\t\n907\t    fingerprint = repair.finding_fingerprint(\n908\t        normalized[0][\"component\"], sorted(f[\"boundary\"] for f in normalized), sorted(f[\"message\"] for f in normalized)\n909\t    )\n910\t    counters = dict(state.get(\"attempt_counters\") or {})\n911\t    repeat_key = _repeat_key(fingerprint)\n912\t    prior_repeats = int(counters.get(repeat_key, 0))\n913\t    if prior_repeats >= MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS:\n914\t        return {\n915\t            \"workbook_finding_partitions\": [\n916\t                {\n917\t                    \"key\": canonical_digest({\"fingerprint\": fingerprint, \"kind\": \"exhausted\"}),\n918\t                    \"component\": normalized[0][\"component\"],\n919\t                    \"findings\": normalized,\n920\t                    \"fingerprint\": fingerprint,\n921\t                }\n922\t            ],\n923\t            \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\", \"convergence_exhausted\", fingerprint=fingerprint),\n924\t            \"terminal_candidate\": {\n925\t                \"kind\": \"CONVERGENCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n926\t                \"bound\": \"fingerprint_bound\",\n927\t                \"counters\": counters,\n928\t                \"fingerprints\": [{\"component\": normalized[0][\"component\"], \"fingerprint\": fingerprint, \"bound\": \"fingerprint_bound\", \"repeats\": prior_repeats}],\n929\t                \"last_findings\": normalized,\n930\t            },\n931\t        }\n932\t\n933\t    attempt_key = _attempt_key(fingerprint)\n934\t    ordinal = int(counters.get(attempt_key, 0)) + 1\n935\t    if ordinal > MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN:\n936\t        return {\n937\t            \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\", \"convergence_exhausted\", ordinal=ordinal),\n938\t            \"terminal_candidate\": {\n939\t                \"kind\": \"CONVERGENCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n940\t                \"bound\": \"attempt_bound\",\n941\t                \"counters\": counters,\n942\t                \"fingerprints\": [fingerprint],\n943\t                \"last_findings\": normalized,\n944\t            },\n945\t        }\n946\t\n947\t    component = normalized[0][\"component\"]\n948\t    # The granted repair boundary is the component's own body section, not the\n949\t    # (possibly page-level) finding pointer that triggered classification: a\n950\t    # `layout`/`assembly` re-render legitimately changes every field under\n951\t    # `/assembly` (the PDF hash included), and a boundary narrower than that\n952\t    # would make `D31`'s own admission check reject the very repair D29 just\n953\t    # authorized.\n954\t    boundary_pointers = [_COMPONENT_BODY_POINTER[component]]\n955\t    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n956\t    require(isinstance(head, Mapping), \"invalid_input\", \"D29 requires a current workbook head\")\n957\t\n958\t    request = {\n959\t        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"fingerprint\": fingerprint, \"attempt\": ordinal}),\n960\t        \"component\": component,\n961\t        \"finding_ids\": [f[\"finding_id\"] for f in normalized],\n962\t        \"boundary\": {\"json_pointers\": boundary_pointers},\n963\t        \"parent_hash\": head[\"hash\"],\n964\t        \"attempt_ordinal\": ordinal,\n965\t        \"fingerprint\": fingerprint,\n966\t        \"prior_repeats\": prior_repeats,\n967\t    }\n968\t\n969\t    partition = {\n970\t        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"fingerprint\": fingerprint, \"kind\": \"partition\"}),\n971\t        \"component\": component,\n972\t        \"findings\": normalized,\n973\t        \"fingerprint\": fingerprint,\n974\t    }\n975\t\n976\t    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n977\t    version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"])\n978\t    require(isinstance(version, Mapping), \"integrity\", \"no admitted workbook version matches the current head\")\n979\t    accepted_unit_hashes = dict(version[\"body\"][\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"])\n980\t\n981\t    update: dict[str, Any] = {\n982\t        \"attempt_counters\": {attempt_key: ordinal},\n983\t        \"workbook_finding_partitions\": [partition],\n984\t        \"workbook_repair_requests\": [request],\n985\t    }\n986\t\n987\t    if component in DETERMINISTIC_ONLY_COMPONENTS:\n988\t        # Both deterministic-only components (`layout`, the rendered page set,\n989\t        # and `assembly`, the workbook PDF itself) are re-derived by\n990\t        # re-rendering `body[\"assembly\"]` from the *unchanged* accepted unit\n991\t        # hashes; neither ever touches `body[\"coverage\"]`, which is the one\n992\t        # section a workbook repair boundary must never name (spec section\n993\t        # 12: workbook repair cannot stage a writable unit source or PDF).\n994\t        new_body = dict(version[\"body\"])\n995\t        new_body[\"assembly\"] = {**version[\"body\"][\"assembly\"], \"repaired\": True, \"repaired_component\": component}\n996\t        candidate = {\n997\t            \"key\": canonical_digest({\"request_key\": request[\"key\"], \"kind\": \"deterministic_candidate\"}),\n998\t            \"record_kind\": DETERMINISTIC_REPAIR_CANDIDATE_KIND,\n999\t            \"request_key\": request[\"key\"],\n1000\t            \"component\": component,\n1001\t            \"parent_sha256\": head[\"hash\"],\n1002\t            \"body\": new_body,\n1003\t        }\n1004\t        update[\"workbook_versions\"] = [candidate]\n1005\t        update[\"pending_guard\"] = _guard(\n1006\t            \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\", \"deterministic_repair\", request_key=request[\"key\"]\n1007\t        )\n1008\t        return update\n1009\t\n1010\t    require(component in MODEL_ONLY_COMPONENTS, \"integrity\", f\"component {component!r} has no dispatch rule\")\n1011\t    packet = worker_packet(\n1012\t        run_id=state.get(\"run_id\"),\n1013\t        episode_id=state.get(\"episode_id\"),\n1014\t        correlation_key=f\"{request['key']}/M08\",\n1015\t        projection={\n1016\t            \"defect\": {\n1017\t                \"defect_id\": request[\"key\"],\n1018\t                \"component\": component,\n1019\t                \"findings\": [\n1020\t                    {\"finding_id\": f[\"finding_id\"], \"pointer\": f[\"boundary\"], \"message\": f[\"message\"]}\n1021\t                    for f in normalized\n1022\t                ],\n1023\t            },\n1024\t            \"parent\": {\n1025\t                \"artifact_name\": f\"workbook:{component}\",\n1026\t                \"artifact_body\": canonical_digest(version[\"body\"]),\n1027\t                \"parent_sha256\": head[\"hash\"],\n1028\t            },\n1029\t            \"allowed_files\": {\"files\": [f\"{component}.json\"]},\n1030\t            \"accepted_unit_hashes\": accepted_unit_hashes,\n1031\t            \"workbook_pdf_hash\": version[\"body\"][\"assembly\"][\"workbook_pdf_sha256\"],\n1032\t            \"invalidated_descendants\": [\"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\"],\n1033\t            \"retest_order\": [\"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\"],\n1034\t        },\n1035\t    )\n1036\t    update[\"pending_packet\"] = staged_dispatch(\"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\", [packet])\n1037\t    update[\"pending_guard\"] = _guard(\n1038\t        \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\", \"model_repair\", request_key=request[\"key\"]\n1039\t    )\n1040\t    return update\n1041\t\n1042\t\n1043\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1044\t# D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\n1045\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1046\t\n1047\t\n1048\tdef D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n1049\t    \"\"\"Admit a boundary-checked workbook child, or refuse it as a system fault.\n1050\t\n1051\t    Recomputes the parent/child diff itself and, before anything else, proves\n1052\t    every accepted unit's frozen PDF hash the parent named is still exactly\n1053\t    the hash the child names: workbook repair can never stage a writable unit\n1054\t    source or PDF (spec section 12), so any unit-hash drift here is always\n1055\t    `SystemFailure`, never a routed finding.\n1056\t    \"\"\"\n1057\t\n1058\t    requests = [record for record in state.get(\"workbook_repair_requests\") or [] if isinstance(record, Mapping)]\n1059\t    require(bool(requests), \"invalid_input\", \"D31 requires a routed repair request\")\n1060\t    request = requests[-1]\n1061\t    boundary = request[\"boundary\"][\"json_pointers\"]\n1062\t\n1063\t    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n1064\t    require(isinstance(head, Mapping), \"invalid_input\", \"D31 requires a current workbook head\")\n1065\t    parent_version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"])\n1066\t    require(isinstance(parent_version, Mapping), \"integrity\", \"no admitted workbook version matches the current head\")\n1067\t    parent_body = parent_version[\"body\"]\n1068\t\n1069\t    model_candidate = _latest_model_repair_candidate(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"))\n1070\t    deterministic_candidate = _latest_deterministic_repair_candidate(\n1071\t        state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), request_key=request[\"key\"]\n1072\t    )\n1073\t    require(\n1074\t        (model_candidate is not None) != (deterministic_candidate is not None),\n1075\t        \"join\",\n1076\t        \"D31 requires exactly one pending repair candidate: model or deterministic\",\n1077\t    )\n1078\t\n1079\t    if model_candidate is not None:\n1080\t        payload = candidate_payload(model_candidate, \"M08 repair candidate\")\n1081\t        child = payload.get(\"candidate_child\")\n1082\t        require(isinstance(child, Mapping), \"schema_contract\", \"M08 candidate carries no candidate_child\")\n1083\t        component = request[\"component\"]\n1084\t        new_body = dict(parent_body)\n1085\t        new_body[component] = {**parent_body[component], \"repaired_by\": \"M08\", \"addressed_defect_id\": child.get(\"addressed_defect_id\")}\n1086\t        declared_parent_sha = model_candidate.get(\"parent_sha256\")\n1087\t    else:\n1088\t        new_body = deterministic_candidate[\"body\"]\n1089\t        declared_parent_sha = deterministic_candidate.get(\"parent_sha256\")\n1090\t\n1091\t    require(\n1092\t        declared_parent_sha == head[\"hash\"],\n1093\t        \"integrity\",\n1094\t        \"the repair candidate's declared parent is not the current workbook head (stale repair)\",\n1095\t        declared=declared_parent_sha,\n1096\t        current=head[\"hash\"],\n1097\t    )\n1098\t\n1099\t    # The unit-hash immutability guard: recomputed before anything else is\n1100\t    # admitted, over the *actual* current accepted receipts, never the\n1101\t    # candidate's own claim.\n1102\t    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n1103\t    for unit_id, pdf_sha256 in parent_body[\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"].items():\n1104\t        receipt = accepted.get(unit_id)\n1105\t        current_pdf = _accepted_pdf_hash(receipt, unit_id) if isinstance(receipt, Mapping) else None\n1106\t        require(\n1107\t            current_pdf == pdf_sha256,\n1108\t            \"integrity\",\n1109\t            \"workbook repair observed a changed accepted unit hash\",\n1110\t            unit_id=unit_id,\n1111\t        )\n1112\t    child_pdf_hashes = new_body.get(\"coverage\", {}).get(\"unit_pdf_hashes\", {})\n1113\t    require(\n1114\t        dict(child_pdf_hashes) == dict(parent_body[\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"]),\n1115\t        \"integrity\",\n1116\t        \"a workbook repair candidate changed an accepted unit's hash\",\n1117\t        parent=parent_body[\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"],\n1118\t        child=child_pdf_hashes,\n1119\t    )\n1120\t\n1121\t    diff = repair.json_pointer_diff(parent_body, new_body)\n1122\t    require(bool(diff), \"integrity\", \"a workbook repair candidate makes no change (in-place, no-op repair)\")\n1123\t    out_of_bound = sorted(pointer for pointer in diff if not repair.within_boundary(pointer, boundary))\n1124\t    require(\n1125\t        not out_of_bound,\n1126\t        \"integrity\",\n1127\t        \"a workbook repair candidate changed bytes outside its declared boundary\",\n1128\t        out_of_bound=out_of_bound,\n1129\t        boundary=boundary,\n1130\t    )\n1131\t\n1132\t    child_record = {\n1133\t        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"kind\": \"workbook_version\", \"body\": new_body, \"parent\": head[\"hash\"]}),\n1134\t        \"record_kind\": None,\n1135\t        \"version\": int(head[\"version\"]) + 1,\n1136\t        \"parent_hash\": head[\"hash\"],\n1137\t        \"hash\": canonical_digest(new_body),\n1138\t        \"body\": new_body,\n1139\t        \"request_key\": request[\"key\"],\n1140\t        \"component\": request[\"component\"],\n1141\t    }\n1142\t\n1143\t    retest = {\n1144\t        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"request_key\": request[\"key\"], \"kind\": \"workbook_retest\"}),\n1145\t        \"request_key\": request[\"key\"],\n1146\t        \"component\": request[\"component\"],\n1147\t        \"destination\": \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\",\n1148\t        \"resolved\": True,\n1149\t    }\n1150\t\n1151\t    return {\n1152\t        \"workbook_versions\": [child_record],\n1153\t        \"workbook_head\": {\n1154\t            WORKBOOK_STREAM: {\n1155\t                \"version\": child_record[\"version\"],\n1156\t                \"parent_hash\": child_record[\"parent_hash\"],\n1157\t                \"hash\": child_record[\"hash\"],\n1158\t            }\n1159\t        },\n1160\t        \"workbook_retests\": [retest],\n1161\t        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n1162\t            \"D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\", \"workbook_repair_admitted\", request_key=request[\"key\"]\n1163\t        ),\n1164\t    }\n1165\t\n1166\t\n1167\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1168\t# D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\n1169\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1170\t\n1171\t\n1172\tdef D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n1173\t    \"\"\"Recompute the final release audit against current bytes; release, or repair.\n1174\t\n1175\t    Never trusts D28's earlier pass label -- a retest that changed a head, or\n1176\t    an accepted receipt that went stale, between D28 and D32 makes this\n1177\t    recomputation fail even though D28 once passed. Only D32 can authorize\n1178\t    `COMPLETE`, and it does so from freshly recomputed evidence (spec section\n1179\t    13.2's closing sentence).\n1180\t    \"\"\"\n1181\t\n1182\t    result = compute_workbook_denominator(state)\n1183\t    audit = {\n1184\t        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"kind\": \"final_release_audit\", \"categories\": result.denominator}),\n1185\t        \"result\": \"PASS\" if result.passed else \"FAIL\",\n1186\t        \"categories\": result.denominator,\n1187\t    }\n1188\t\n1189\t    if not result.passed:\n1190\t        return {\n1191\t            \"final_release_audits\": [audit],\n1192\t            \"deterministic_checks\": [result.check],\n1193\t            \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n1194\t                \"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\", \"workbook_repairable\", findings=result.findings\n1195\t            ),\n1196\t        }\n1197\t\n1198\t    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n1199\t    version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"])\n1200\t    effective_run = state.get(\"effective_run\") or {}\n1201\t    ordered = list(effective_run.get(\"ordered_unit_ids\") or [])\n1202\t    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n1203\t    checkpoints = state.get(\"checkpoint_metadata\") or []\n1204\t    require(bool(checkpoints), \"integrity\", \"D32 requires a current checkpoint correlation\")\n1205\t\n1206\t    audit = {**audit, \"workbook_hash\": head[\"hash\"]}\n1207\t    candidate = {\n1208\t        \"kind\": \"COMPLETE\",\n1209\t        \"release_audit_key\": audit[\"key\"],\n1210\t        \"workbook_hash\": head[\"hash\"],\n1211\t        \"coverage\": {\"ordered_unit_ids\": ordered, \"unit_pdf_hashes\": version[\"body\"][\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"]},\n1212\t        \"unit_receipt_hashes\": {unit_id: accepted[unit_id][\"receipt_hash\"] for unit_id in ordered},\n1213\t        \"log_high_water_mark\": len(state.get(\"evidence_index_entries\") or []),\n1214\t        \"checkpoint_id\": checkpoints[-1].get(\"checkpoint_id\"),\n1215\t    }\n1216\t\n1217\t    return {\n1218\t        \"final_release_audits\": [audit],\n1219\t        \"deterministic_checks\": [result.check],\n1220\t        \"terminal_candidate\": candidate,\n1221\t        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\", \"release_proven\"),\n1222\t    }\n1223\t\n1224\t\n1225\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1226\t# Topology registration (spec section 8.1's workbook branch)\n1227\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1228\t#\n1229\t# Additive registration over the one builder N20/N30 already populated, in the\n1230\t# same convention `unit_graph.register_unit_path` uses: no `add_node`, no\n1231\t# `StateGraph()`, no `compile()`. D90/D91 are deliberately absent from this\n1232\t# module's own `add_conditional_edges` calls -- both are shared bookkeeping\n1233\t# nodes `unit_graph.py` already registers a branch for, and re-registering the\n1234\t# same source under a different branch name would double-fire on every\n1235\t# execution (LangGraph attaches every branch of a node as an independent\n1236\t# writer). `D90`'s dispatch to `M07`/`M08` reaches them anyway: the guard\n1237\t#(`routing.route_attempt_reservation`) returns `Send` objects for an\n1238\t# authorized dispatch, and a `Send` target bypasses the registered branch's\n1239\t# `path_map` entirely, so the pre-existing narrower `ends` unit_graph.py froze\n1240\t# never has to name a workbook job to reach one.\n1241\t\n1242\t\n1243\tWORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES: Mapping[str, Any] = {\n1244\t    \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\": D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE,\n1245\t    \"D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\": D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK,\n1246\t    \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\": D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK,\n1247\t    \"D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\": D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET,\n1248\t    \"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\": D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE,\n1249\t    \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\": D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR,\n1250\t    \"D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\": D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR,\n1251\t    \"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\": D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE,\n1252\t}\n1253\t\n1254\t\n1255\tdef _routing() -> Any:\n1256\t    from . import routing\n1257\t\n1258\t    return routing\n1259\t\n1260\t\n1261\t# (source node id, guard callable name on `routing`) -- resolved lazily via\n1262\t# `_routing()` so this module does not import `routing` at module scope\n1263\t# (avoiding a cycle is unnecessary here, but keeping the same lazy-import\n1264\t# convention `unit_graph.py`/`acceptance.py` already use for cross-module\n1265\t# helpers keeps this file's import graph uniform).\n1266\tWORKBOOK_TOPOLOGY_SOURCES: tuple[str, ...] = (\n1267\t    \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\",\n1268\t    \"D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\",\n1269\t    \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\",\n1270\t    \"D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\",\n1271\t    \"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\",\n1272\t    \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\",\n1273\t    \"D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\",\n1274\t    \"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\",\n1275\t    \"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\",\n1276\t    \"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\",\n1277\t)\n1278\t\n1279\t\n1280\tdef register_workbook_path(builder: Any, available: Sequence[str]) -> dict[str, tuple[str, ...]]:\n1281\t    \"\"\"Add the workbook branch's own outgoing edges to the shared builder.\n1282\t\n1283\t    Called by `graph.py` after `unit_graph.register_unit_path`, over the same\n1284\t    `StateGraph` instance -- every node this module names as a source must\n1285\t    already be `add_node`-registered by the caller. Returns the resolved\n1286\t    per-source destination map so a caller can assert the registered topology\n1287\t    the way `unit_graph.register_unit_path` already does.\n1288\t    \"\"\"\n1289\t\n1290\t    routing = _routing()\n1291\t    available_set = set(available)\n1292\t    for node_id in WORKBOOK_TOPOLOGY_SOURCES:\n1293\t        if node_id not in available_set:\n1294\t            raise routing.RoutingViolation(\n1295\t                f\"N32-EDGE-DANGLING:{node_id}: the workbook path names a node with no registered body\"\n1296\t            )\n1297\t\n1298\t    guards: dict[str, Any] = {\n1299\t        \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\": routing.route_manifest_coverage,\n1300\t        \"D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\": routing.route_workbook_assembly,\n1301\t        \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\": routing.route_workbook_inspection,\n1302\t        \"D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\": routing.route_workbook_packet,\n1303\t        \"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\": routing.route_workbook_reduction,\n1304\t        \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\": routing.route_workbook_repair_plan,\n1305\t        \"D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\": routing.route_workbook_repair_admission,\n1306\t        \"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\": routing.route_final_release,\n1307\t        \"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\": routing.route_m07_workbook_review,\n1308\t        \"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\": routing.route_m08_workbook_repair,\n1309\t    }\n1310\t\n1311\t    # `routing.guard_destinations()` resolves a *deterministic* node's own\n1312\t    # `GUARD_DESTINATIONS` row, which D24-D32 all have. M07/M08 are model\n1313\t    # *result* sources instead: their success destination lives in\n1314\t    # `routing.MODEL_RESULT_DESTINATIONS`, a table `guard_destinations()`\n1315\t    # does not consult (the same reason `unit_graph.py` declares M01/M02/M03/\n1316\t    # M05's destinations explicitly rather than deriving them generically).\n1317\t    model_result_extra: Mapping[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {\n1318\t        \"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\": (routing.MODEL_RESULT_DESTINATIONS[\"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\"],),\n1319\t        \"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\": (routing.MODEL_RESULT_DESTINATIONS[\"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\"],),\n1320\t    }\n1321\t\n1322\t    resolved: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {}\n1323\t    for source in WORKBOOK_TOPOLOGY_SOURCES:\n1324\t        path = guards[source]\n1325\t        declared = set(routing.guard_destinations(source)) | set(model_result_extra.get(source, ()))\n1326\t        destinations = tuple(sorted(declared & available_set))\n1327\t        if not destinations:\n1328\t            raise routing.RoutingViolation(f\"N32-EDGE-EMPTY:{source}: every declared destination is deferred\")\n1329\t        builder.add_conditional_edges(source, path, {target: target for target in destinations})\n1330\t        resolved[source] = destinations\n1331\t    return resolved\n1332\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18d83993-700d-4340-bec9-cb55c092357d","uuid":"dc98cc43-1c2b-4099-8574-c2216cd28853","timestamp":"2026-08-12T21:52:22.721Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/attempt-20260812T215023.910830Z-53d2cc5b32/repo/runtime/langgraph_factory/workbook.py","content":"\"\"\"Workbook assembly, review, repair, and release: D24-D32 of spec section 6.2.\n\nThis is the one workbook engine (spec section 15's `node_ownership.v1.md`\nresolution): exact manifest coverage (D24), assembly (D25), render/inventory/\ninspection (D26), review-packet freeze (D27), evidence reduction (D28),\nworkbook-only defect classification/planning (D29), admission/retest (D31),\nand final release recomputation (D32) -- plus the two product-terminal call\nsites `D24` (one-mode `UNIT_ACCEPTED`) and `D32` (`COMPLETE`) reach.\n\nLike `repair.py`/`acceptance.py`, none of these functions carries a\n`NODE_CATALOGUE` row: D24-D32 are not narrowed by `nodes.deterministic_node()`\nand are registered into the compiled graph by `register_workbook_path()`\nbelow, called from `graph.py`. A product terminal is never written here --\n`D24`/`D32` only ever produce a `terminal_candidate` and a `pending_guard`\nthat routes to the one real `D98_WRITE_TERMINAL` (owned by\n`nodes/terminal.py`); this module contains no terminal writer and cannot\nreach `END` directly.\n\nWorkbook repair is boundary-scoped to the four workbook-owned components\n(`front_matter`, `navigation`, `layout`, `assembly` -- `model_nodes\n.WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS`) and can never stage a writable unit source or\nPDF: `D31` recomputes and compares every accepted unit's frozen PDF hash\nbefore and after a repair candidate is admitted, and any change is a system\nfailure, never a routed finding (spec section 12: \"Workbook repair cannot\nstage writable unit sources or PDFs\").\n\nOnly `D30_CLASSIFY_PREREQUISITE` (owned by N22's `nodes/sources.py`) may ever\npropose `PAUSED_PREREQUISITE`; nothing in this module does, and `D98`\nindependently re-derives every candidate's precondition regardless of which\nguard proposed it.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections.abc import Mapping, Sequence\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom . import repair\nfrom .nodes import (\n    SystemFailure,\n    canonical_digest,\n    candidate_payload,\n    check_record,\n    contract_reference,\n    require,\n    sha256_file,\n    staged_dispatch,\n    stream_id,\n    worker_packet,\n)\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"WORKBOOK_STREAM\",\n    \"WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS\",\n    \"DETERMINISTIC_ONLY_COMPONENTS\",\n    \"MODEL_ONLY_COMPONENTS\",\n    \"WorkbookDenominatorResult\",\n    \"compute_workbook_denominator\",\n    \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\",\n    \"D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\",\n    \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\",\n    \"D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\",\n    \"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\",\n    \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\",\n    \"D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\",\n    \"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\",\n    \"WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES\",\n    \"WORKBOOK_TOPOLOGY_SOURCES\",\n    \"register_workbook_path\",\n]\n\n\n# The one workbook stream: unlike a unit, there is exactly one workbook per\n# episode, so `workbook_head`/`workbook_versions` key on this single name\n# rather than a per-entity stream id the way `nodes.stream_id` mints one.\nWORKBOOK_STREAM = \"workbook\"\n\nWORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS: frozenset[str] = frozenset(\n    {\"front_matter\", \"navigation\", \"layout\", \"assembly\"}\n)\n\n# Spec section 12's workbook row: \"deterministic assembly/template repair\n# first; M08 only for the exact workbook-owned component\". `layout` and\n# `assembly` are the two components a deterministic re-render/re-assemble can\n# regenerate outright (the same renderer D25 already calls); `front_matter`\n# and `navigation` are authored text with no deterministic producer in this\n# generation, so they are M08-eligible. This mirrors unit repair's\n# `DETERMINISTIC_ONLY_OWNERS`/`MODEL_ONLY_OWNERS` split (`repair.py`) rather\n# than inventing a second policy shape.\nDETERMINISTIC_ONLY_COMPONENTS: frozenset[str] = frozenset({\"layout\", \"assembly\"})\nMODEL_ONLY_COMPONENTS: frozenset[str] = frozenset({\"front_matter\", \"navigation\"})\n\nDETERMINISTIC_REPAIR_CANDIDATE_KIND = \"deterministic_workbook_repair_candidate\"\n\n# The one body section each workbook-owned component's repair is scoped to.\n# `layout` and `assembly` share `/assembly` deliberately (spec section 12:\n# both are re-rendered together); `/coverage` -- the accepted-unit hash\n# ledger -- is named by no component, which is exactly the unit-byte\n# immutability guarantee D31 also re-derives independently.\n_COMPONENT_BODY_POINTER: dict[str, str] = {\n    \"front_matter\": \"/front_matter\",\n    \"navigation\": \"/navigation\",\n    \"layout\": \"/assembly\",\n    \"assembly\": \"/assembly\",\n}\n\n# Frozen limits reused from the one repair engine (spec section 12: \"shared\n# boundary/diff/invalidation-DAG machinery reused by workbook repair\") --\n# never redeclared with a different value here.\nMAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = repair.MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN\nMAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS = repair.MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS\n\n\ndef _guard(node_id: str, value: str, **detail: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\"node\": node_id, \"value\": value, \"detail\": detail}\n\n\ndef _record(value: Any, label: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    require(isinstance(value, Mapping), \"schema_contract\", f\"{label} must be a JSON object\")\n    return dict(value)\n\n\ndef _accepted_pdf_hash(receipt: Any, unit_id: str) -> str:\n    require(isinstance(receipt, Mapping), \"integrity\", f\"unit {unit_id!r} has no accepted receipt\")\n    pages = ((receipt.get(\"denominator\") or {}).get(\"pages\")) or {}\n    pdf_sha256 = pages.get(\"pdf_sha256\")\n    require(\n        isinstance(pdf_sha256, str) and bool(pdf_sha256),\n        \"integrity\",\n        f\"the accepted receipt for {unit_id!r} carries no frozen unit pdf hash\",\n    )\n    return pdf_sha256\n\n\ndef _latest_workbook_version(workbook_versions: Any, workbook_hash: str) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n    matches = [\n        dict(record)\n        for record in workbook_versions or []\n        if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n        and record.get(\"hash\") == workbook_hash\n        and record.get(\"record_kind\") is None\n    ]\n    return matches[-1] if matches else None\n\n\ndef _latest_model_repair_candidate(workbook_versions: Any) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n    matches = [\n        dict(record)\n        for record in workbook_versions or []\n        if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n        and record.get(\"record_kind\") == \"model_candidate\"\n        and record.get(\"job_id\") == \"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\"\n    ]\n    return matches[-1] if matches else None\n\n\ndef _latest_deterministic_repair_candidate(\n    workbook_versions: Any, *, request_key: str\n) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n    matches = [\n        dict(record)\n        for record in workbook_versions or []\n        if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n        and record.get(\"record_kind\") == DETERMINISTIC_REPAIR_CANDIDATE_KIND\n        and record.get(\"request_key\") == request_key\n    ]\n    return matches[-1] if matches else None\n\n\ndef _latest_workbook_review(workbook_reviews: Any, workbook_pdf_sha256: str | None) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n    if not workbook_pdf_sha256:\n        return None\n    matches = [\n        dict(record)\n        for record in workbook_reviews or []\n        if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n        and record.get(\"record_kind\") == \"model_candidate\"\n        and record.get(\"job_id\") == \"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\"\n        and record.get(\"workbook_pdf_sha256\") == workbook_pdf_sha256\n    ]\n    return matches[-1] if matches else None\n\n\ndef _attempt_key(fingerprint: str) -> str:\n    return f\"workbook_repair|{fingerprint}\"\n\n\ndef _repeat_key(fingerprint: str) -> str:\n    return f\"workbook_repeat|{fingerprint}\"\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"One-mode unit terminal, or all-mode exact ordered coverage proof.\"\"\"\n\n    mode = state.get(\"mode\")\n    require(mode in (\"one\", \"all\"), \"invalid_input\", \"D24 requires a decided run mode\")\n\n    effective_run = state.get(\"effective_run\") or {}\n    closure = list(effective_run.get(\"target_closure\") or [])\n    require(bool(closure), \"invalid_input\", \"D24 requires a non-empty frozen target closure\")\n    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n\n    missing = [unit_id for unit_id in closure if unit_id not in accepted]\n    require(\n        not missing,\n        \"integrity\",\n        \"D24 requires an accepted receipt for every unit in the frozen closure\",\n        missing=missing,\n    )\n\n    if mode == \"one\":\n        requested = state.get(\"requested_unit_id\")\n        require(\n            isinstance(requested, str) and requested in accepted,\n            \"integrity\",\n            \"the requested unit has no accepted receipt\",\n            requested_unit_id=requested,\n        )\n        require(requested in closure, \"integrity\", \"the requested unit is outside the frozen closure\")\n        receipt = accepted[requested]\n        checkpoints = state.get(\"checkpoint_metadata\") or []\n        require(bool(checkpoints), \"integrity\", \"D24 requires a current checkpoint correlation\")\n        checkpoint_id = checkpoints[-1].get(\"checkpoint_id\")\n\n        candidate = {\n            \"kind\": \"UNIT_ACCEPTED\",\n            \"unit_id\": requested,\n            \"receipt_hash\": receipt[\"receipt_hash\"],\n            \"closure_receipt_hashes\": {unit_id: accepted[unit_id][\"receipt_hash\"] for unit_id in closure},\n            \"denominator\": receipt[\"denominator\"],\n            \"log_high_water_mark\": len(state.get(\"evidence_index_entries\") or []),\n            \"checkpoint_id\": checkpoint_id,\n        }\n        return {\n            \"terminal_candidate\": candidate,\n            \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n                \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\", \"unit_target_accepted\", unit_id=requested\n            ),\n        }\n\n    ordered = list(effective_run.get(\"ordered_unit_ids\") or [])\n    require(bool(ordered), \"invalid_input\", \"D24 requires a non-empty frozen manifest order\")\n    require(\n        sorted(ordered) == sorted(closure) and len(ordered) == len(closure),\n        \"integrity\",\n        \"full-mode manifest order and target closure disagree\",\n        ordered=ordered,\n        closure=closure,\n    )\n\n    declared_coverage = [{\"unit_id\": unit_id, \"receipt_hash\": accepted[unit_id][\"receipt_hash\"]} for unit_id in ordered]\n    ok, rejections = repair_acceptance_coverage_proof(ordered, accepted, declared_coverage)\n    require(ok, \"integrity\", \"exact manifest coverage failed\", rejections=rejections)\n\n    coverage_record = {\n        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"kind\": \"workbook_coverage\", \"ordered_unit_ids\": ordered, \"declared_coverage\": declared_coverage}),\n        \"ordered_unit_ids\": ordered,\n        \"receipt_hashes\": {unit_id: accepted[unit_id][\"receipt_hash\"] for unit_id in ordered},\n    }\n    return {\n        \"workbook_coverage\": [coverage_record],\n        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n            \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\", \"manifest_coverage_proven\", ordered_unit_ids=ordered\n        ),\n    }\n\n\ndef repair_acceptance_coverage_proof(\n    ordered_unit_ids: Sequence[str],\n    accepted_unit_receipts: Mapping[str, Any],\n    declared_coverage: Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]],\n) -> tuple[bool, list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"The exact coverage predicate (spec section 13.2 item 1), applied at D24.\n\n    Delegates to N31's `acceptance.prove_exact_manifest_coverage` -- one\n    coverage rule, not a second copy of it -- imported lazily to avoid a\n    module cycle (`acceptance.py` itself imports `repair`, and this module\n    imports `repair` at top level).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    from . import acceptance\n\n    return acceptance.prove_exact_manifest_coverage(\n        list(ordered_unit_ids), accepted_unit_receipts, list(declared_coverage)\n    )\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Assemble the workbook over exact accepted receipts and immutable unit PDFs.\n\n    Never mutates a unit: every unit PDF byte this reads is re-verified against\n    the hash the unit's own accepted receipt froze, both the version D25 sees\n    in state and the actual bytes on disk, before assembly proceeds.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    coverage_entries = [\n        record for record in state.get(\"workbook_coverage\") or [] if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n    ]\n    require(bool(coverage_entries), \"invalid_input\", \"D25 requires a proven coverage record\")\n    coverage = coverage_entries[-1]\n    ordered = list(coverage[\"ordered_unit_ids\"])\n    receipt_hashes = dict(coverage[\"receipt_hashes\"])\n    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n    artifact_versions = state.get(\"artifact_versions\") or []\n\n    unit_pdf_hashes: dict[str, str] = {}\n    for unit_id in ordered:\n        receipt = accepted.get(unit_id)\n        require(\n            isinstance(receipt, Mapping) and receipt.get(\"receipt_hash\") == receipt_hashes.get(unit_id),\n            \"integrity\",\n            \"the proven coverage receipt hash is not the current accepted receipt\",\n            unit_id=unit_id,\n        )\n        accepted_pdf_sha256 = _accepted_pdf_hash(receipt, unit_id)\n\n        layout_stream = stream_id(unit_id, \"layout\")\n        layout_candidates = [\n            dict(record)\n            for record in artifact_versions\n            if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"stream\") == layout_stream\n        ]\n        require(bool(layout_candidates), \"integrity\", f\"no rendered layout exists for accepted unit {unit_id!r}\")\n        layout_version = max(layout_candidates, key=lambda record: record.get(\"version\", 0))\n        require(\n            layout_version.get(\"pdf_sha256\") == accepted_pdf_sha256,\n            \"integrity\",\n            \"unit PDF bytes changed after acceptance\",\n            unit_id=unit_id,\n            accepted=accepted_pdf_sha256,\n            current=layout_version.get(\"pdf_sha256\"),\n        )\n        pdf_path = Path(str(layout_version.get(\"pdf_path\")))\n        require(pdf_path.is_file(), \"integrity\", \"the accepted unit PDF is missing\", unit_id=unit_id)\n        actual = sha256_file(pdf_path)\n        require(\n            actual == accepted_pdf_sha256,\n            \"integrity\",\n            \"the unit PDF bytes on disk no longer match the accepted hash\",\n            unit_id=unit_id,\n        )\n        unit_pdf_hashes[unit_id] = accepted_pdf_sha256\n\n    engine_root = state.get(\"engine_root\")\n    front_matter = contract_reference(engine_root, \"meta_prompt/assets/pedagogy.v1.md\")\n\n    registry = getattr(runtime_context, \"transport_registry\", None)\n    assembler = getattr(registry, \"assemble_workbook\", None) if registry else None\n    require(callable(assembler), \"capability\", \"runtime context exposes no workbook assembler\")\n    try:\n        assembled = assembler(ordered, unit_pdf_hashes, front_matter)\n    except Exception as error:  # noqa: BLE001 - a tool fault is always a system failure\n        raise SystemFailure(\n            \"tool\", f\"workbook assembly failed: {error}\", {\"ordered_unit_ids\": ordered}\n        ) from error\n\n    result = _record(assembled, \"workbook assembly result\")\n    for field in (\"workbook_pdf_path\", \"workbook_pdf_sha256\", \"assembly_map\", \"navigation\"):\n        require(field in result, \"integrity\", f\"workbook assembly result has no {field!r}\")\n    assembly_map = result[\"assembly_map\"]\n    require(\n        isinstance(assembly_map, list) and [entry.get(\"unit_id\") for entry in assembly_map] == ordered,\n        \"integrity\",\n        \"the assembly map is not exactly the proven coverage order\",\n        expected=ordered,\n    )\n    for entry in assembly_map:\n        entry_record = _record(entry, \"assembly map entry\")\n        require(\n            entry_record.get(\"unit_pdf_sha256\") == unit_pdf_hashes.get(entry_record.get(\"unit_id\")),\n            \"integrity\",\n            \"the assembly map cites a unit pdf hash the coverage did not prove\",\n            unit_id=entry_record.get(\"unit_id\"),\n        )\n\n    body = {\n        \"front_matter\": front_matter,\n        \"navigation\": result[\"navigation\"],\n        \"coverage\": {\"ordered_unit_ids\": ordered, \"unit_pdf_hashes\": unit_pdf_hashes},\n        \"assembly\": {\n            \"assembly_map\": assembly_map,\n            \"workbook_pdf_path\": result[\"workbook_pdf_path\"],\n            \"workbook_pdf_sha256\": result[\"workbook_pdf_sha256\"],\n        },\n    }\n\n    current_head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM) or {}\n    version_record = {\n        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"kind\": \"workbook_version\", \"body\": body, \"parent\": current_head.get(\"hash\")}),\n        \"record_kind\": None,\n        \"version\": int(current_head.get(\"version\", 0)) + 1,\n        \"parent_hash\": current_head.get(\"hash\"),\n        \"hash\": canonical_digest(body),\n        \"body\": body,\n    }\n\n    return {\n        \"workbook_versions\": [version_record],\n        \"workbook_head\": {\n            WORKBOOK_STREAM: {\n                \"version\": version_record[\"version\"],\n                \"parent_hash\": version_record[\"parent_hash\"],\n                \"hash\": version_record[\"hash\"],\n            }\n        },\n        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\", \"workbook_assembled\"),\n    }\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Prove a positive contiguous workbook page inventory and inspect every page.\"\"\"\n\n    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n    require(isinstance(head, Mapping), \"invalid_input\", \"D26 requires an assembled workbook head\")\n    version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"])\n    require(isinstance(version, Mapping), \"integrity\", \"no admitted workbook version matches the current head\")\n\n    assembly = version[\"body\"][\"assembly\"]\n    pdf_sha256 = assembly[\"workbook_pdf_sha256\"]\n    pdf_path = Path(str(assembly[\"workbook_pdf_path\"]))\n    require(pdf_path.is_file(), \"integrity\", \"the assembled workbook PDF is missing\")\n    actual = sha256_file(pdf_path)\n    require(\n        actual == pdf_sha256,\n        \"integrity\",\n        \"the workbook PDF bytes changed after assembly\",\n        declared=pdf_sha256,\n        actual=actual,\n    )\n\n    registry = getattr(runtime_context, \"transport_registry\", None)\n    inspector = getattr(registry, \"inspect_workbook_pages\", None) if registry else None\n    require(callable(inspector), \"capability\", \"runtime context exposes no workbook page inspector\")\n    try:\n        inspected = inspector(str(pdf_path), pdf_sha256)\n    except Exception as error:  # noqa: BLE001 - a rasterizer/tool fault is always a system failure\n        raise SystemFailure(\n            \"tool\", f\"workbook page inspection failed: {error}\", {\"pdf_sha256\": pdf_sha256}\n        ) from error\n\n    report = _record(inspected, \"workbook page inspection\")\n    pages = report.get(\"pages\")\n    require(isinstance(pages, list), \"schema_contract\", \"workbook page inspection returned a non-list page set\")\n\n    numbers = [page.get(\"number\") for page in pages if isinstance(page, Mapping)]\n    contiguous = numbers == list(range(1, len(pages) + 1))\n    positive = len(pages) > 0\n\n    inventory = {\n        \"key\": f\"workbook/{pdf_sha256}\",\n        \"pdf_sha256\": pdf_sha256,\n        \"page_count\": len(pages),\n        \"contiguous\": contiguous,\n        \"result\": \"PASS\" if positive and contiguous else \"FAIL\",\n    }\n\n    inspections: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    findings: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    if not (positive and contiguous):\n        findings.append(\n            {\n                \"component\": \"layout\",\n                \"check_id\": \"workbook_page_inventory\",\n                \"pointer\": \"/assembly/pages\",\n                \"message\": \"page inventory is empty\" if not positive else f\"page numbering is not 1..N: {numbers}\",\n            }\n        )\n\n    for page in pages:\n        page_record = _record(page, \"workbook page inspection entry\")\n        number = page_record.get(\"number\")\n        problems = sorted(str(item) for item in page_record.get(\"problems\", []) or [])\n        if bool(page_record.get(\"unreadable\")):\n            problems = sorted({*problems, \"unreadable\"})\n        page_sha256 = page_record.get(\"page_sha256\")\n        require(\n            isinstance(page_sha256, str) and len(page_sha256) == 64,\n            \"integrity\",\n            f\"workbook page {number} was inspected without a page hash\",\n        )\n        image_path = page_record.get(\"image_path\")\n        require(\n            isinstance(image_path, str) and bool(image_path),\n            \"integrity\",\n            f\"workbook page {number} was inspected without a rendered page image\",\n        )\n        inspections.append(\n            {\n                \"key\": f\"workbook/{pdf_sha256}/{number}\",\n                \"pdf_sha256\": pdf_sha256,\n                \"page\": number,\n                \"page_sha256\": page_sha256,\n                \"image_path\": image_path,\n                \"problems\": problems,\n                \"result\": \"PASS\" if not problems else \"FAIL\",\n            }\n        )\n        if problems:\n            findings.append(\n                {\n                    \"component\": \"layout\",\n                    \"check_id\": \"workbook_page_inspection\",\n                    \"pointer\": f\"/assembly/pages/{number}\",\n                    \"message\": f\"workbook page {number} failed inspection: {problems}\",\n                }\n            )\n\n    check = check_record(\n        scope=\"workbook\",\n        owner=WORKBOOK_STREAM,\n        head_hash=pdf_sha256,\n        check_id=\"workbook_pages_inspected\",\n        attempt=version.get(\"version\", 1),\n        result=\"PASS\" if not findings else \"FAIL\",\n        detail={\"page_count\": len(pages), \"finding_count\": len(findings)},\n    )\n\n    value = \"workbook_pages_inspected\" if not findings else \"workbook_layout_repairable\"\n    return {\n        \"workbook_page_inventories\": [inventory],\n        \"workbook_page_inspections\": inspections,\n        \"deterministic_checks\": [check],\n        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n            \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\", value, findings=findings\n        ),\n    }\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Freeze the immutable workbook review packet, exactly every page included.\"\"\"\n\n    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n    require(isinstance(head, Mapping), \"invalid_input\", \"D27 requires an assembled workbook head\")\n    version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"])\n    require(isinstance(version, Mapping), \"integrity\", \"no admitted workbook version matches the current head\")\n    body = version[\"body\"]\n\n    inventories = [\n        record\n        for record in state.get(\"workbook_page_inventories\") or []\n        if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"pdf_sha256\") == body[\"assembly\"][\"workbook_pdf_sha256\"]\n    ]\n    require(bool(inventories), \"invalid_input\", \"D27 requires a current workbook page inventory\")\n    inventory = max(inventories, key=lambda record: record.get(\"page_count\", 0))\n    pdf_sha256 = inventory[\"pdf_sha256\"]\n\n    inspections = sorted(\n        (\n            record\n            for record in state.get(\"workbook_page_inspections\") or []\n            if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"pdf_sha256\") == pdf_sha256\n        ),\n        key=lambda record: record.get(\"page\", 0),\n    )\n    page_numbers = [record.get(\"page\") for record in inspections]\n    require(\n        page_numbers == list(range(1, inventory[\"page_count\"] + 1)),\n        \"join\",\n        \"the frozen packet's page set is not exactly the inventory's pages\",\n        expected=inventory[\"page_count\"],\n        actual=page_numbers,\n    )\n\n    pdf_path = Path(str(body[\"assembly\"][\"workbook_pdf_path\"]))\n    require(pdf_path.is_file(), \"integrity\", \"the shipped workbook PDF is missing\")\n    actual = sha256_file(pdf_path)\n    require(\n        actual == pdf_sha256,\n        \"integrity\",\n        \"the shipped workbook PDF bytes do not match the inventoried hash\",\n    )\n\n    checks = [\n        record\n        for record in state.get(\"deterministic_checks\") or []\n        if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"scope\") == \"workbook\"\n    ]\n\n    rubric_path = Path(str(state.get(\"engine_root\"))) / \"meta_prompt\" / \"assets\" / \"pedagogy.v1.md\"\n    rubric = {\"path\": str(rubric_path), \"sha256\": sha256_file(rubric_path) if rubric_path.is_file() else None}\n    require(rubric[\"sha256\"] is not None, \"schema_contract\", \"the workbook review rubric is missing\")\n\n    coverage_entries = [\n        record for record in state.get(\"workbook_coverage\") or [] if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n    ]\n    require(bool(coverage_entries), \"invalid_input\", \"D27 requires a proven coverage record\")\n    coverage = coverage_entries[-1]\n\n    packet = {\n        \"coverage_map\": {\n            \"ordered_unit_ids\": list(coverage[\"ordered_unit_ids\"]),\n            \"receipt_hashes\": dict(coverage[\"receipt_hashes\"]),\n        },\n        \"accepted_unit_hashes\": dict(body[\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"]),\n        \"workbook_pdf_sha256\": pdf_sha256,\n        \"page_count\": inventory[\"page_count\"],\n        \"page_keys\": [record[\"key\"] for record in inspections],\n        \"deterministic_check_keys\": sorted(\n            f\"{record['scope']}/{record['owner']}/{record['head_hash']}/{record['check_id']}/{record['attempt']}\"\n            for record in checks\n        ),\n        \"rubric\": rubric,\n    }\n    packet[\"denominator\"] = {\"pages\": inventory[\"page_count\"], \"checks\": len(packet[\"deterministic_check_keys\"])}\n    packet[\"key\"] = canonical_digest(packet)\n    packet[\"packet_hash\"] = packet[\"key\"]\n\n    page_records = []\n    for record in inspections:\n        page_records.append(\n            {\n                \"page_number\": record[\"page\"],\n                \"page_sha256\": record[\"page_sha256\"],\n                \"image_path\": record[\"image_path\"],\n            }\n        )\n\n    review_worker_packet = worker_packet(\n        run_id=state.get(\"run_id\"),\n        episode_id=state.get(\"episode_id\"),\n        correlation_key=f\"workbook/{pdf_sha256}/review\",\n        projection={\n            \"coverage_map\": dict(packet[\"coverage_map\"]),\n            \"accepted_unit_hashes\": dict(packet[\"accepted_unit_hashes\"]),\n            \"workbook_pdf\": {\"sha256\": pdf_sha256, \"path\": str(pdf_path)},\n            \"page_inventory\": {\n                \"page_count\": inventory[\"page_count\"],\n                \"pages\": [\n                    {\"page_number\": entry[\"page_number\"], \"page_sha256\": entry[\"page_sha256\"]}\n                    for entry in page_records\n                ],\n            },\n            \"pages\": page_records,\n            \"deterministic_evidence\": [\n                {\n                    \"check_id\": record[\"check_id\"],\n                    \"scope\": record[\"scope\"],\n                    \"head_hash\": record[\"head_hash\"],\n                    \"result\": record[\"result\"],\n                }\n                for record in checks\n            ],\n            \"rubric\": dict(rubric),\n        },\n    )\n\n    return {\n        \"workbook_review_packets\": [packet],\n        \"pending_packet\": staged_dispatch(\"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\", [review_worker_packet]),\n        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\", \"workbook_packet_frozen\"),\n    }\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Denominator (shared shape by D28 and D32 -- spec section 13.2)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass WorkbookDenominatorResult:\n    __slots__ = (\"passed\", \"check\", \"findings\", \"denominator\")\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        passed: bool,\n        check: dict[str, Any],\n        findings: list[dict[str, Any]],\n        denominator: dict[str, Any],\n    ) -> None:\n        self.passed = passed\n        self.check = check\n        self.findings = findings\n        self.denominator = denominator\n\n\ndef compute_workbook_denominator(state: Mapping[str, Any]) -> WorkbookDenominatorResult:\n    \"\"\"Recompute the complete current workbook denominator (spec section 13.2).\n\n    Never trusts a cached pass label: every category below is re-derived from\n    the *current* state on every call, exactly as `acceptance\n    .compute_unit_denominator` does for a unit -- a stale head, a superseded\n    review, or an unresolved workbook repair request all fail this function\n    freshly regardless of what an earlier call over older state returned.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    findings: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    categories: dict[str, Any] = {}\n\n    def _fail(component: str, check_id: str, pointer: str, message: str) -> None:\n        findings.append({\"check_id\": check_id, \"component\": component, \"pointer\": pointer, \"message\": message})\n\n    effective_run = state.get(\"effective_run\") or {}\n    ordered = list(effective_run.get(\"ordered_unit_ids\") or [])\n    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n    coverage_entries = [record for record in state.get(\"workbook_coverage\") or [] if isinstance(record, Mapping)]\n    coverage = coverage_entries[-1] if coverage_entries else None\n\n    coverage_ok = (\n        coverage is not None\n        and list(coverage.get(\"ordered_unit_ids\") or []) == ordered\n        and bool(ordered)\n        and all(\n            isinstance(accepted.get(unit_id), Mapping)\n            and accepted[unit_id].get(\"receipt_hash\") == coverage.get(\"receipt_hashes\", {}).get(unit_id)\n            for unit_id in ordered\n        )\n    )\n    categories[\"coverage\"] = {\"result\": \"PASS\" if coverage_ok else \"FAIL\"}\n    if not coverage_ok:\n        _fail(\"assembly\", \"workbook_coverage\", \"/coverage\", \"current coverage is not exact ordered full-manifest membership\")\n\n    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n    version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"]) if isinstance(head, Mapping) else None\n    unit_bytes_ok = coverage_ok and version is not None\n    if unit_bytes_ok:\n        for unit_id, pdf_sha256 in version[\"body\"][\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"].items():\n            receipt = accepted.get(unit_id)\n            if not isinstance(receipt, Mapping) or ((receipt.get(\"denominator\") or {}).get(\"pages\") or {}).get(\"pdf_sha256\") != pdf_sha256:\n                unit_bytes_ok = False\n                break\n    categories[\"unit_bytes\"] = {\"result\": \"PASS\" if unit_bytes_ok else \"FAIL\"}\n    if not unit_bytes_ok:\n        _fail(\"assembly\", \"workbook_unit_bytes\", \"/assembly\", \"an accepted unit's PDF bytes are not the assembled workbook's frozen bytes\")\n\n    pdf_sha256 = version[\"body\"][\"assembly\"][\"workbook_pdf_sha256\"] if version is not None else None\n    inventories = [\n        record\n        for record in state.get(\"workbook_page_inventories\") or []\n        if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"pdf_sha256\") == pdf_sha256\n    ]\n    inventory = max(inventories, key=lambda record: record.get(\"page_count\", 0)) if inventories else None\n    inventory_ok = isinstance(inventory, Mapping) and inventory.get(\"result\") == \"PASS\"\n    inspections = [\n        record\n        for record in state.get(\"workbook_page_inspections\") or []\n        if isinstance(record, Mapping) and record.get(\"pdf_sha256\") == pdf_sha256\n    ]\n    expected_pages = inventory.get(\"page_count\") if isinstance(inventory, Mapping) else -1\n    pages_ok = inventory_ok and len(inspections) == expected_pages and all(record.get(\"result\") == \"PASS\" for record in inspections)\n    categories[\"pages\"] = {\"result\": \"PASS\" if pages_ok else \"FAIL\", \"pdf_sha256\": pdf_sha256, \"page_count\": expected_pages}\n    if not pages_ok:\n        _fail(\"layout\", \"workbook_pages\", \"/assembly/pages\", \"the workbook page inventory/inspection set is not current and fully passing\")\n\n    review = _latest_workbook_review(state.get(\"workbook_reviews\"), pdf_sha256)\n    review_ok = review is not None\n    if review is not None:\n        payload = candidate_payload(review, \"workbook review\")\n        blocking = [\n            entry for entry in payload.get(\"overall_findings\", [])\n            if isinstance(entry, Mapping) and entry.get(\"severity\") == \"blocking\"\n        ]\n        for page_entry in payload.get(\"page_findings\", []):\n            if isinstance(page_entry, Mapping):\n                blocking.extend(\n                    entry for entry in page_entry.get(\"findings\", [])\n                    if isinstance(entry, Mapping) and entry.get(\"severity\") == \"blocking\"\n                )\n        for entry in blocking:\n            component = str(entry.get(\"category\") or \"layout\")\n            component = component if component in WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS else \"layout\"\n            findings.append(\n                {\n                    \"check_id\": \"workbook_review_finding\",\n                    \"component\": component,\n                    \"pointer\": entry.get(\"evidence_reference\") or \"/review\",\n                    \"message\": entry.get(\"description\", \"\"),\n                }\n            )\n        review_ok = not blocking\n    categories[\"review\"] = {\"result\": \"PASS\" if review_ok else \"FAIL\", \"present\": review is not None}\n    if review is None:\n        _fail(\"navigation\", \"workbook_review_missing\", \"/review\", \"no independent workbook review candidate is present for the current pdf\")\n\n    open_requests = [\n        record\n        for record in state.get(\"workbook_repair_requests\") or []\n        if isinstance(record, Mapping)\n        and record.get(\"key\")\n        not in {\n            entry.get(\"request_key\")\n            for entry in state.get(\"workbook_retests\") or []\n            if isinstance(entry, Mapping) and entry.get(\"resolved\")\n        }\n    ]\n    repair_ok = not open_requests\n    categories[\"repair\"] = {\"result\": \"PASS\" if repair_ok else \"FAIL\", \"open_requests\": len(open_requests)}\n    if not repair_ok:\n        _fail(open_requests[0][\"component\"], \"workbook_repair_unresolved\", \"/repair\", \"a workbook repair request remains open (not yet retested)\")\n\n    passed = all(entry.get(\"result\") == \"PASS\" for entry in categories.values())\n    summary_hash = canonical_digest({\"kind\": \"workbook_denominator\", \"categories\": categories})\n    check = check_record(\n        scope=\"workbook\",\n        owner=WORKBOOK_STREAM,\n        head_hash=summary_hash,\n        check_id=\"workbook_denominator\",\n        attempt=1,\n        result=\"PASS\" if passed else \"FAIL\",\n        detail={\"categories\": categories},\n    )\n    return WorkbookDenominatorResult(passed, check, findings, categories)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Build the complete current workbook denominator; release, or open repair.\"\"\"\n\n    result = compute_workbook_denominator(state)\n    if result.passed:\n        return {\n            \"deterministic_checks\": [result.check],\n            \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\", \"workbook_denominator_passed\"),\n        }\n    return {\n        \"deterministic_checks\": [result.check],\n        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n            \"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\", \"workbook_findings_repairable\", findings=result.findings\n        ),\n    }\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Classify the current workbook-only findings and plan exactly one repair.\n\n    Merges spec 6.2's D17/D18/D19 roles into the one row the workbook branch\n    declares: total classification, one planned request, and deterministic-vs-\n    model routing, all against the single `WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS`\n    vocabulary rather than the five-owner unit table.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    guard_record = state.get(\"pending_guard\")\n    pending_failure = state.get(\"pending_failure\")\n\n    if isinstance(pending_failure, Mapping) and pending_failure.get(\"classification\") == \"repair\":\n        detail = pending_failure.get(\"evidence\") if isinstance(pending_failure.get(\"evidence\"), Mapping) else {}\n        raw_findings = [\n            {\n                \"component\": \"front_matter\",\n                \"check_id\": pending_failure.get(\"failure_class\"),\n                \"pointer\": \"/front_matter\",\n                \"message\": pending_failure.get(\"detail\") or pending_failure.get(\"message\") or \"\",\n            }\n        ]\n        source_node = \"D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE\"\n    else:\n        require(isinstance(guard_record, Mapping), \"invalid_input\", \"D29 has no findings to classify\")\n        detail = guard_record.get(\"detail\") if isinstance(guard_record.get(\"detail\"), Mapping) else {}\n        raw_findings = detail.get(\"findings\")\n        require(\n            isinstance(raw_findings, list) and bool(raw_findings),\n            \"invalid_input\",\n            \"D29 was routed with an empty or missing findings list\",\n        )\n        source_node = str(guard_record.get(\"node\") or \"\")\n\n    normalized: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for raw in raw_findings:\n        raw_record = _record(raw, \"workbook finding\")\n        component = raw_record.get(\"component\")\n        require(\n            component in WORKBOOK_OWNED_COMPONENTS,\n            \"invalid_input\",\n            f\"workbook finding declares component {component!r}, which is not one of the four workbook-owned components\",\n        )\n        pointer = raw_record.get(\"pointer\")\n        require(isinstance(pointer, str) and bool(pointer), \"invalid_input\", \"workbook finding declares no boundary pointer\")\n        message = raw_record.get(\"message\", \"\")\n        normalized.append(\n            {\n                \"finding_id\": canonical_digest({\"component\": component, \"pointer\": pointer, \"message\": str(message)}),\n                \"component\": component,\n                \"boundary\": pointer,\n                \"message\": str(message),\n                \"source_node\": source_node,\n            }\n        )\n\n    fingerprint = repair.finding_fingerprint(\n        normalized[0][\"component\"], sorted(f[\"boundary\"] for f in normalized), sorted(f[\"message\"] for f in normalized)\n    )\n    counters = dict(state.get(\"attempt_counters\") or {})\n    repeat_key = _repeat_key(fingerprint)\n    prior_repeats = int(counters.get(repeat_key, 0))\n    if prior_repeats >= MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS:\n        return {\n            \"workbook_finding_partitions\": [\n                {\n                    \"key\": canonical_digest({\"fingerprint\": fingerprint, \"kind\": \"exhausted\"}),\n                    \"component\": normalized[0][\"component\"],\n                    \"findings\": normalized,\n                    \"fingerprint\": fingerprint,\n                }\n            ],\n            \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\", \"convergence_exhausted\", fingerprint=fingerprint),\n            \"terminal_candidate\": {\n                \"kind\": \"CONVERGENCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n                \"bound\": \"fingerprint_bound\",\n                \"counters\": counters,\n                \"fingerprints\": [{\"component\": normalized[0][\"component\"], \"fingerprint\": fingerprint, \"bound\": \"fingerprint_bound\", \"repeats\": prior_repeats}],\n                \"last_findings\": normalized,\n            },\n        }\n\n    attempt_key = _attempt_key(fingerprint)\n    ordinal = int(counters.get(attempt_key, 0)) + 1\n    if ordinal > MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN:\n        return {\n            \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\", \"convergence_exhausted\", ordinal=ordinal),\n            \"terminal_candidate\": {\n                \"kind\": \"CONVERGENCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n                \"bound\": \"attempt_bound\",\n                \"counters\": counters,\n                \"fingerprints\": [fingerprint],\n                \"last_findings\": normalized,\n            },\n        }\n\n    component = normalized[0][\"component\"]\n    # The granted repair boundary is the component's own body section, not the\n    # (possibly page-level) finding pointer that triggered classification: a\n    # `layout`/`assembly` re-render legitimately changes every field under\n    # `/assembly` (the PDF hash included), and a boundary narrower than that\n    # would make `D31`'s own admission check reject the very repair D29 just\n    # authorized.\n    boundary_pointers = [_COMPONENT_BODY_POINTER[component]]\n    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n    require(isinstance(head, Mapping), \"invalid_input\", \"D29 requires a current workbook head\")\n\n    request = {\n        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"fingerprint\": fingerprint, \"attempt\": ordinal}),\n        \"component\": component,\n        \"finding_ids\": [f[\"finding_id\"] for f in normalized],\n        \"boundary\": {\"json_pointers\": boundary_pointers},\n        \"parent_hash\": head[\"hash\"],\n        \"attempt_ordinal\": ordinal,\n        \"fingerprint\": fingerprint,\n        \"prior_repeats\": prior_repeats,\n    }\n\n    partition = {\n        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"fingerprint\": fingerprint, \"kind\": \"partition\"}),\n        \"component\": component,\n        \"findings\": normalized,\n        \"fingerprint\": fingerprint,\n    }\n\n    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n    version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"])\n    require(isinstance(version, Mapping), \"integrity\", \"no admitted workbook version matches the current head\")\n    accepted_unit_hashes = dict(version[\"body\"][\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"])\n\n    update: dict[str, Any] = {\n        \"attempt_counters\": {attempt_key: ordinal},\n        \"workbook_finding_partitions\": [partition],\n        \"workbook_repair_requests\": [request],\n    }\n\n    if component in DETERMINISTIC_ONLY_COMPONENTS:\n        # Both deterministic-only components (`layout`, the rendered page set,\n        # and `assembly`, the workbook PDF itself) are re-derived by\n        # re-rendering `body[\"assembly\"]` from the *unchanged* accepted unit\n        # hashes; neither ever touches `body[\"coverage\"]`, which is the one\n        # section a workbook repair boundary must never name (spec section\n        # 12: workbook repair cannot stage a writable unit source or PDF).\n        new_body = dict(version[\"body\"])\n        new_body[\"assembly\"] = {**version[\"body\"][\"assembly\"], \"repaired\": True, \"repaired_component\": component}\n        candidate = {\n            \"key\": canonical_digest({\"request_key\": request[\"key\"], \"kind\": \"deterministic_candidate\"}),\n            \"record_kind\": DETERMINISTIC_REPAIR_CANDIDATE_KIND,\n            \"request_key\": request[\"key\"],\n            \"component\": component,\n            \"parent_sha256\": head[\"hash\"],\n            \"body\": new_body,\n        }\n        update[\"workbook_versions\"] = [candidate]\n        update[\"pending_guard\"] = _guard(\n            \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\", \"deterministic_repair\", request_key=request[\"key\"]\n        )\n        return update\n\n    require(component in MODEL_ONLY_COMPONENTS, \"integrity\", f\"component {component!r} has no dispatch rule\")\n    packet = worker_packet(\n        run_id=state.get(\"run_id\"),\n        episode_id=state.get(\"episode_id\"),\n        correlation_key=f\"{request['key']}/M08\",\n        projection={\n            \"defect\": {\n                \"defect_id\": request[\"key\"],\n                \"component\": component,\n                \"findings\": [\n                    {\"finding_id\": f[\"finding_id\"], \"pointer\": f[\"boundary\"], \"message\": f[\"message\"]}\n                    for f in normalized\n                ],\n            },\n            \"parent\": {\n                \"artifact_name\": f\"workbook:{component}\",\n                \"artifact_body\": canonical_digest(version[\"body\"]),\n                \"parent_sha256\": head[\"hash\"],\n            },\n            \"allowed_files\": {\"files\": [f\"{component}.json\"]},\n            \"accepted_unit_hashes\": accepted_unit_hashes,\n            \"workbook_pdf_hash\": version[\"body\"][\"assembly\"][\"workbook_pdf_sha256\"],\n            \"invalidated_descendants\": [\"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\"],\n            \"retest_order\": [\"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\"],\n        },\n    )\n    update[\"pending_packet\"] = staged_dispatch(\"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\", [packet])\n    update[\"pending_guard\"] = _guard(\n        \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\", \"model_repair\", request_key=request[\"key\"]\n    )\n    return update\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Admit a boundary-checked workbook child, or refuse it as a system fault.\n\n    Recomputes the parent/child diff itself and, before anything else, proves\n    every accepted unit's frozen PDF hash the parent named is still exactly\n    the hash the child names: workbook repair can never stage a writable unit\n    source or PDF (spec section 12), so any unit-hash drift here is always\n    `SystemFailure`, never a routed finding.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    requests = [record for record in state.get(\"workbook_repair_requests\") or [] if isinstance(record, Mapping)]\n    require(bool(requests), \"invalid_input\", \"D31 requires a routed repair request\")\n    request = requests[-1]\n    boundary = request[\"boundary\"][\"json_pointers\"]\n\n    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n    require(isinstance(head, Mapping), \"invalid_input\", \"D31 requires a current workbook head\")\n    parent_version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"])\n    require(isinstance(parent_version, Mapping), \"integrity\", \"no admitted workbook version matches the current head\")\n    parent_body = parent_version[\"body\"]\n\n    model_candidate = _latest_model_repair_candidate(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"))\n    deterministic_candidate = _latest_deterministic_repair_candidate(\n        state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), request_key=request[\"key\"]\n    )\n    require(\n        (model_candidate is not None) != (deterministic_candidate is not None),\n        \"join\",\n        \"D31 requires exactly one pending repair candidate: model or deterministic\",\n    )\n\n    if model_candidate is not None:\n        payload = candidate_payload(model_candidate, \"M08 repair candidate\")\n        child = payload.get(\"candidate_child\")\n        require(isinstance(child, Mapping), \"schema_contract\", \"M08 candidate carries no candidate_child\")\n        component = request[\"component\"]\n        new_body = dict(parent_body)\n        new_body[component] = {**parent_body[component], \"repaired_by\": \"M08\", \"addressed_defect_id\": child.get(\"addressed_defect_id\")}\n        declared_parent_sha = model_candidate.get(\"parent_sha256\")\n    else:\n        new_body = deterministic_candidate[\"body\"]\n        declared_parent_sha = deterministic_candidate.get(\"parent_sha256\")\n\n    require(\n        declared_parent_sha == head[\"hash\"],\n        \"integrity\",\n        \"the repair candidate's declared parent is not the current workbook head (stale repair)\",\n        declared=declared_parent_sha,\n        current=head[\"hash\"],\n    )\n\n    # The unit-hash immutability guard: recomputed before anything else is\n    # admitted, over the *actual* current accepted receipts, never the\n    # candidate's own claim.\n    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n    for unit_id, pdf_sha256 in parent_body[\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"].items():\n        receipt = accepted.get(unit_id)\n        current_pdf = _accepted_pdf_hash(receipt, unit_id) if isinstance(receipt, Mapping) else None\n        require(\n            current_pdf == pdf_sha256,\n            \"integrity\",\n            \"workbook repair observed a changed accepted unit hash\",\n            unit_id=unit_id,\n        )\n    child_pdf_hashes = new_body.get(\"coverage\", {}).get(\"unit_pdf_hashes\", {})\n    require(\n        dict(child_pdf_hashes) == dict(parent_body[\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"]),\n        \"integrity\",\n        \"a workbook repair candidate changed an accepted unit's hash\",\n        parent=parent_body[\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"],\n        child=child_pdf_hashes,\n    )\n\n    diff = repair.json_pointer_diff(parent_body, new_body)\n    require(bool(diff), \"integrity\", \"a workbook repair candidate makes no change (in-place, no-op repair)\")\n    out_of_bound = sorted(pointer for pointer in diff if not repair.within_boundary(pointer, boundary))\n    require(\n        not out_of_bound,\n        \"integrity\",\n        \"a workbook repair candidate changed bytes outside its declared boundary\",\n        out_of_bound=out_of_bound,\n        boundary=boundary,\n    )\n\n    child_record = {\n        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"kind\": \"workbook_version\", \"body\": new_body, \"parent\": head[\"hash\"]}),\n        \"record_kind\": None,\n        \"version\": int(head[\"version\"]) + 1,\n        \"parent_hash\": head[\"hash\"],\n        \"hash\": canonical_digest(new_body),\n        \"body\": new_body,\n        \"request_key\": request[\"key\"],\n        \"component\": request[\"component\"],\n    }\n\n    retest = {\n        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"request_key\": request[\"key\"], \"kind\": \"workbook_retest\"}),\n        \"request_key\": request[\"key\"],\n        \"component\": request[\"component\"],\n        \"destination\": \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\",\n        \"resolved\": True,\n    }\n\n    return {\n        \"workbook_versions\": [child_record],\n        \"workbook_head\": {\n            WORKBOOK_STREAM: {\n                \"version\": child_record[\"version\"],\n                \"parent_hash\": child_record[\"parent_hash\"],\n                \"hash\": child_record[\"hash\"],\n            }\n        },\n        \"workbook_retests\": [retest],\n        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n            \"D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\", \"workbook_repair_admitted\", request_key=request[\"key\"]\n        ),\n    }\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE(state: Mapping[str, Any], runtime_context: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Recompute the final release audit against current bytes; release, or repair.\n\n    Never trusts D28's earlier pass label -- a retest that changed a head, or\n    an accepted receipt that went stale, between D28 and D32 makes this\n    recomputation fail even though D28 once passed. Only D32 can authorize\n    `COMPLETE`, and it does so from freshly recomputed evidence (spec section\n    13.2's closing sentence).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    result = compute_workbook_denominator(state)\n    audit = {\n        \"key\": canonical_digest({\"kind\": \"final_release_audit\", \"categories\": result.denominator}),\n        \"result\": \"PASS\" if result.passed else \"FAIL\",\n        \"categories\": result.denominator,\n    }\n\n    if not result.passed:\n        return {\n            \"final_release_audits\": [audit],\n            \"deterministic_checks\": [result.check],\n            \"pending_guard\": _guard(\n                \"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\", \"workbook_repairable\", findings=result.findings\n            ),\n        }\n\n    head = (state.get(\"workbook_head\") or {}).get(WORKBOOK_STREAM)\n    version = _latest_workbook_version(state.get(\"workbook_versions\"), head[\"hash\"])\n    effective_run = state.get(\"effective_run\") or {}\n    ordered = list(effective_run.get(\"ordered_unit_ids\") or [])\n    accepted = state.get(\"accepted_unit_receipts\") or {}\n    checkpoints = state.get(\"checkpoint_metadata\") or []\n    require(bool(checkpoints), \"integrity\", \"D32 requires a current checkpoint correlation\")\n\n    audit = {**audit, \"workbook_hash\": head[\"hash\"]}\n    candidate = {\n        \"kind\": \"COMPLETE\",\n        \"release_audit_key\": audit[\"key\"],\n        \"workbook_hash\": head[\"hash\"],\n        \"coverage\": {\"ordered_unit_ids\": ordered, \"unit_pdf_hashes\": version[\"body\"][\"coverage\"][\"unit_pdf_hashes\"]},\n        \"unit_receipt_hashes\": {unit_id: accepted[unit_id][\"receipt_hash\"] for unit_id in ordered},\n        \"log_high_water_mark\": len(state.get(\"evidence_index_entries\") or []),\n        \"checkpoint_id\": checkpoints[-1].get(\"checkpoint_id\"),\n    }\n\n    return {\n        \"final_release_audits\": [audit],\n        \"deterministic_checks\": [result.check],\n        \"terminal_candidate\": candidate,\n        \"pending_guard\": _guard(\"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\", \"release_proven\"),\n    }\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Topology registration (spec section 8.1's workbook branch)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n#\n# Additive registration over the one builder N20/N30 already populated, in the\n# same convention `unit_graph.register_unit_path` uses: no `add_node`, no\n# `StateGraph()`, no `compile()`. D90/D91 are deliberately absent from this\n# module's own `add_conditional_edges` calls -- both are shared bookkeeping\n# nodes `unit_graph.py` already registers a branch for, and re-registering the\n# same source under a different branch name would double-fire on every\n# execution (LangGraph attaches every branch of a node as an independent\n# writer). `D90`'s dispatch to `M07`/`M08` reaches them anyway: the guard\n#(`routing.route_attempt_reservation`) returns `Send` objects for an\n# authorized dispatch, and a `Send` target bypasses the registered branch's\n# `path_map` entirely, so the pre-existing narrower `ends` unit_graph.py froze\n# never has to name a workbook job to reach one.\n\n\nWORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES: Mapping[str, Any] = {\n    \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\": D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE,\n    \"D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\": D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK,\n    \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\": D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK,\n    \"D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\": D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET,\n    \"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\": D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE,\n    \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\": D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR,\n    \"D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\": D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR,\n    \"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\": D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE,\n}\n\n\ndef _routing() -> Any:\n    from . import routing\n\n    return routing\n\n\n# (source node id, guard callable name on `routing`) -- resolved lazily via\n# `_routing()` so this module does not import `routing` at module scope\n# (avoiding a cycle is unnecessary here, but keeping the same lazy-import\n# convention `unit_graph.py`/`acceptance.py` already use for cross-module\n# helpers keeps this file's import graph uniform).\nWORKBOOK_TOPOLOGY_SOURCES: tuple[str, ...] = (\n    \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\",\n    \"D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\",\n    \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\",\n    \"D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\",\n    \"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\",\n    \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\",\n    \"D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\",\n    \"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\",\n    \"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\",\n    \"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\",\n)\n\n\ndef register_workbook_path(builder: Any, available: Sequence[str]) -> dict[str, tuple[str, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"Add the workbook branch's own outgoing edges to the shared builder.\n\n    Called by `graph.py` after `unit_graph.register_unit_path`, over the same\n    `StateGraph` instance -- every node this module names as a source must\n    already be `add_node`-registered by the caller. Returns the resolved\n    per-source destination map so a caller can assert the registered topology\n    the way `unit_graph.register_unit_path` already does.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    routing = _routing()\n    available_set = set(available)\n    for node_id in WORKBOOK_TOPOLOGY_SOURCES:\n        if node_id not in available_set:\n            raise routing.RoutingViolation(\n                f\"N32-EDGE-DANGLING:{node_id}: the workbook path names a node with no registered body\"\n            )\n\n    guards: dict[str, Any] = {\n        \"D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE\": routing.route_manifest_coverage,\n        \"D25_ASSEMBLE_WORKBOOK\": routing.route_workbook_assembly,\n        \"D26_RENDER_INVENTORY_INSPECT_WORKBOOK\": routing.route_workbook_inspection,\n        \"D27_FREEZE_WORKBOOK_REVIEW_PACKET\": routing.route_workbook_packet,\n        \"D28_REDUCE_WORKBOOK_EVIDENCE\": routing.route_workbook_reduction,\n        \"D29_CLASSIFY_AND_PLAN_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\": routing.route_workbook_repair_plan,\n        \"D31_ADMIT_AND_RETEST_WORKBOOK_REPAIR\": routing.route_workbook_repair_admission,\n        \"D32_RECOMPUTE_FINAL_RELEASE\": routing.route_final_release,\n        \"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\": routing.route_m07_workbook_review,\n        \"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\": routing.route_m08_workbook_repair,\n    }\n\n    # `routing.guard_destinations()` resolves a *deterministic* node's own\n    # `GUARD_DESTINATIONS` row, which D24-D32 all have. M07/M08 are model\n    # *result* sources instead: their success destination lives in\n    # `routing.MODEL_RESULT_DESTINATIONS`, a table `guard_destinations()`\n    # does not consult (the same reason `unit_graph.py` declares M01/M02/M03/\n    # M05's destinations explicitly rather than deriving them generically).\n    model_result_extra: Mapping[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {\n        \"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\": (routing.MODEL_RESULT_DESTINATIONS[\"M07_REVIEW_ACTUAL_WORKBOOK\"],),\n        \"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\": (routing.MODEL_RESULT_DESTINATIONS[\"M08_REPAIR_NAMED_WORKBOOK_DEFECT\"],),\n    }\n\n    resolved: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {}\n    for source in WORKBOOK_TOPOLOGY_SOURCES:\n        path = guards[source]\n        declared = set(routing.guard_destinations(source)) | set(model_result_extra.get(source, ()))\n        destinations = tuple(sorted(declared & available_set))\n        if not destinations:\n            raise routing.RoutingViolation(f\"N32-EDGE-EMPTY:{source}: every declared destination is deferred\")\n        builder.add_conditional_edges(source, path, {target: target for target in destinations})\n        resolved[source] = destinations\n    return resolved\n","numLines":1332,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1332}}}
